{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire","id":1075440,"title":"Reasons to run 1st edition Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-09T05:24:32-07:00","id":1075440,"title":"Reasons to run 1st edition Vampire","content":"Now here is my conundrum.<br /> <br /> I have been a collector of nWoD (CoD now) all my RPGing days, the largest part of the collection has always been VtR. Despite this and my love for the material I never got an opportunity to run or play in a VtR game, it has always been either straight up blue book games or HtV. So those books have been sitting on the shelf, read but never played.<br /> <br /> Now however I've got a group that is finally interested in playing Vampires and I'm at a crossroads. I've been running the 2nd edition CoD rules for the last few years and have the VtR 2nd edition ruleset. I've been loving changes to the core system but I feel a longing to play the 1st edition ones and use them at least once.<br /> <br /> In the end I'll probably just run the 2nd edition rules, as this group are used to the CoD system, but I'm interested in hearing from those who have run and played both version.<br /> <br /> In your opinion, are they any reasons to play 1st edition over 2nd edition beyond simple nostalgia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/6Xp5aea.png?1\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/nEEA0aK.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6021-jin-keota","name":"Jin Keota","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6021_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T06:04:03-07:00","id":1075444,"title":"","content":"Not really. The second edition is such a great improvement it seems weird anyone would have both and consciously decide to run first edition instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T06:26:04-07:00","id":1075450,"title":"","content":"&quot;Because I feel like it once in awhile&quot; is a perfectly good enough reason, I'd say.<br /> <br /> I could see wanting to get away from the bookkeeping of Conditions once in awhile, or to introduce the base system to a group of new players without that level of detail.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T06:41:37-07:00","id":1075454,"title":"","content":"But for someone who's already familiar with the general 2E changes I'd say that VtR 2E is the better choice for everything except the nostalgia factor. All the vampire specific changes between the editions are just improvements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T07:47:19-07:00","id":1075477,"title":"","content":"While I get the feeling this is a loaded question fishing for an edition war, I'll answer. Yes, there are many reasons to play 1st edition over 2nd edition. It's called personal preference, not nostalgia. Developer bias started creeping in the 1st edition publishings but it is blatant and in your face with 2nd edition. I don't like their &quot;fixes&quot; to the things I considered a problem or could see how/why others considered it a problem. And in fact, they ended up making those problems worse. The power disparity between clans and covenants is wider now to where I can't suspend disbelief. I had to make changes to a lot of the mechanics and ideology. There's also default themes and elements. 2nd ed. is a lot more about rapidly plunging down a nihilistic spiral of self destruction and gaining as much instant temporary gratification along the way. Whereas 1st edition is more about slowly moving toward that end but trying to avoid it while amassing power. I personally liked spending over 8 years of real life gaming time rising from city hound to city regent as did the others I gamed with who moved to similar positions of power but I also realize most people today don't have that kind of attention span. Powers that wear off at the next sunset or get pulled apart by a fledgling Mekhet experimenting with Auspex aren't really conducive to that sort of game play.<br /> <br /> My personal preference also leans toward minimalism. I don't like maintaining a cache of 10 plus dice, five books, charts, cards, tokens, and Excel sheets just to PLAY a character and I don't like having to increase the totals of those things exponentially to RUN a game. Second edition has more rules. You only needed two books for first edition. You currently need four books (one of them technically being 1st edition) if you want to maintain a semblance of balance. Second edition is not very backwards compatible but first is forward compatible. Most of the stuff in 2nd was already in 1st as optional alternative mechanics. They just went from optional to mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-09-2017, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T12:41:03-07:00","id":1075548,"title":"","content":"It really is up to you. One kind of objective reason would be that the immense amount of books that came out for Requiem are for the 1e system, so you can pretty much use them without worrying about compatibility issues. On the other hand, the difference in the systems aren't that big that you can't change minor things to make it fit 2e. All the stuff about the bloodlines is still valid if you use the 1e bloodline system instead of 2e with the boon thingie.<br /> <br /> Personally, my favourite system is a combination of the two editions. I love the little subtleties 2e introduced in the core system, especially the combat, which is now more interesting than a matter of who gets more dice (and defence is now worth investing in). What I don't like is the social maneuvering which I find simply unnecessary and artificial, the touchstone system, which... well it's not so much that I don't like it rather that it simply didn't seem to gel for my players, so we more or less forgot it was there and treated it more as a box on the character sheet to write important NPCs for the PCs. And then there's the conditions. Interesting and pretty good idea, but way too much micromanagement for me and I like to hand out XP at my own rhythm anyway, so I kind of kept it at a minimum (for those conditions that are actually essential to the powers or vampiric condition, like everything linked to disciplines, addiction, frenzy...) and it worked just fine that way.<br /> <br /> So yeah, my suggestion is, since you have both versions, use both to brew the system that really suits your game. They're different enough that each can offer its own advantages, but close enough that it's easy to make the fixes you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:28:01-07:00","id":1075857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1075477#post1075477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I get the feeling this is a loaded question fishing for an edition war, I'll answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>No loaded question here, was just looking for personal input from those who have experience playing/running both. The minimalism point makes sense, played in a few games of Shadowrun 4th edition where you had to have a spreadsheet for each character to deal with all the calculations and tracking. Really used to put damper on games at times. For CoD I've not had to do much more tracking than I did for 1e, at least for mortals. I'll have a look further into 2e and see what I'd have to be using from an ST position.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So yeah, my suggestion is, since you have both versions, use both to brew the system that really suits your game. They're different enough that each can offer its own advantages, but close enough that it's easy to make the fixes you need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might end up going this route if I go with 2e, since a lot of the 1e sourcebooks have some material that I'd want to leave open for myself and my players. I actually like the idea of touchstones as an alternative to just using integrity (which, as is, makes sense for humans but less so for vampires after a certain stage) and the old morality system. <br /> <br /> I guess for the most part I won't know what will work and what won't until I try them out. Hopefully any teething issues won't put the group off trying Vampire in the long term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/6Xp5aea.png?1\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/nEEA0aK.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6021-jin-keota","name":"Jin Keota","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6021_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T09:39:37-07:00","id":1075924,"title":"","content":"I've run a chronicle off and on since around 2009. When 2nd ed came out, I started porting some changes in. Over all I like both Werewolf and Vampire 2nd ed much better than their initial editions. That said, my setting has a lot of the old stuff-- mostly fluff, particularly in terms of the covenants. Thus far I've used social maneuvering, conditions and such very little -- mostly use it as guidelines behind the scenes; the players don't like additional fiddly system stuff. (That said, I like the idea conceptually).<br /> <br /> If you want to play it, play it. But for me, a hybrid of mostly 2nd system and largely 1st setting works pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:52:47-07:00","id":1076011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jin Keota</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire#post1075440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here is my conundrum.<br /> In your opinion, are they any reasons to play 1st edition over 2nd edition beyond simple nostalgia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of books.<br /> <br /> If you like something from the 1st edition more you can change the rules. I play Vampire since Dark Ages and Masquerade (more or less 15 years) and IMHO CoD has the best game balance.<br /> I like most of the changes that have been made, but if you are not sure check yourself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:21:13-07:00","id":1076108,"title":"","content":"ironically, my friends and I played a 1st edition Vampire game last weekend because the ST and I went to school together (haven't seen him in years) and we used to play Requiem 1st edition together and he hasn't played CofD since, so he wasn't as familiar with 2e/Blood and Smoke. So the chief reason is pretty much nostalgia, or unfamiliarity.<br /> <br /> That being said, we did use some 'house rules' for fun's sake based somewhat loosely off 2e, like 'you can choose to get a dramatic failure in order to recover a willpower' but the disciplines were all 1e and there were no conditions.<br /> <br /> CofD/NWoD is extremely plug-and-play. Take what you like from 1e and from 2e and mash it together. It still works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:28:15-07:00","id":1076150,"title":"","content":"The reasons to run 1e Requiem are the same reasons to run a non-current edition of any game. You already have the books, you are more familiar with the rules, more supplement support, nostalgia for the old rules or style, personal preference for the old rules or style. Ultimately, the only reason you need is that you want to. Personally, I significantly prefer 2e, but for those who want to run 1e, for any reason, more power to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:10:29-07:00","id":1076463,"title":"","content":"I agree wholeheartedly with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> .<br /> <br /> There's a very real addition to the 'rules density' that require more bookkeeping and subsystem detail in 2E than 1E that offer a tangible reason to choose 1E over 2E. Setting fluff and power scope* are arbitrary to personal preference, but a 1E game is just more streamlined. <b><i>However</i></b>, if as you stated you and yours are already familiar with 2E systems, then there's no reason to play 1E, and probably <b>a strong argument for 2E</b> if it means learning 1E rules.<br /> <br /> * Bailey theirself said that the power and cost metrics were shifted mid-way through 1E development when dev leadership changed hands, making half of the 1E books designed with shifted goal posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:47:02-07:00","id":1076550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1076463#post1076463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Bailey theirself</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI <b>Rose</b> prefers feminine pronouns (she, her, herself, etc).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:47:50-07:00","id":1076551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1076463#post1076463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Bailey theirself</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">It is public and common knowledge on these forums that Rose Bailey's preferred pronouns are she/her/herself/hers. Do not misgender her, or anyone else who makes their preferred pronouns publicly known.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:30:08-07:00","id":1076573,"title":"","content":"Firstly, I go for months and even years without posting on these forums. What you consider 'public and common' may not necessarily be. If a person changes once, they can change again, including moving to third person (which some <i>people </i>do). I didn't realize a<i><b> neutral </b></i>pronoun was considered an 'attack' or that I was responsible for digging up the last post where someone referred to themselves.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I referred to a post made on the old forums <i>and material (1E) written</i> when <i>a different name was used</i>, and <i>not everyone</i> knows that the names are one and the same person. I <b>deliberately </b>chose a <b>neutral </b>pronoun to side-step<i> any confusion or need to explain/open a discussion as to why it would be different</i>.<br /> <br /> A reminder would have been welcome. An <b>accusation </b>over a <i>neutral </i>term without the benefit of the doubt is just as intolerant as what you've accused me of. I have never, on this forum or previous iterations, been intolerant of anything other than stupidity. I've run a board/game for nearly a decade that has a large percentage of LGBT players who are all respected as they choose.<br /> <br /> I didn't mis-gender anyone, and if you choose to read a <i>neutral </i>pronoun that way, it says more about you than it does about me.<br /> <br /> <b>As a minority myself, I find it offensive in the extreme to be accused of intolerance</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","user":"grey_goose","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:35:07-07:00","id":1076575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1076573#post1076573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, I go for months and even years without posting on these forums. What you consider 'public and common' may not necessarily be. If a person changes once, they can change again, including moving to third person (which some <i>people </i>do). I didn't realize a<i><b> neutral </b></i>pronoun was considered an 'attack' or that I was responsible for digging up the last post where someone referred to themselves.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I referred to a post made on the old forums when <i>a different forum name was used</i>, and <i>not everyone</i> knows that the names are one and the same person. I <b>deliberately </b>chose a <b>neutral </b>pronoun to side-step<i> any confusion or need to explain/open a discussion as to why it would be different</i>.<br /> <br /> A reminder would have been welcome. An <b>accusation </b>over a <i>neutral </i>term without the benefit of the doubt is just as intolerant as what you've accused me of. I have never, on this forum or previous iterations, been intolerant of anything other than stupidity. I've run a board/game for nearly a decade that has a large percentage of LGBT players who are all respected as they choose.<br /> <br /> <b>As a minority myself, I find it offensive in the extreme to be accused of intolerance</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">A reminder is exactly what I gave you. I made no accusation of intolerance, only directed you not to misgender users who make their preferred pronouns publicly known. If you took my reminder as an accusation, please refer to my signature. Please refer as well to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">Forum Rules</a>, which clearly state that disputes between community members and the moderators, web administrators or Onyx Path staff should be handled privately, as should discussion of site policy and moderator actions, and to discuss problems or concerns by use of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\">Contact Us</a> link.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-11-2017, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:45:25-07:00","id":1076583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grey_goose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1076463#post1076463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree wholeheartedly with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5466_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5466\" data-vbnamecard=\"5466\">tsusasi</a> .<br /> <br /> There's a very real addition to the 'rules density' that require more bookkeeping and subsystem detail in 2E than 1E that offer a tangible reason to choose 1E over 2E. Setting fluff and power scope* are arbitrary to personal preference, but a 1E game is just more streamlined. <b><i>However</i></b>, if as you stated you and yours are already familiar with 2E systems, then there's no reason to play 1E, and probably <b>a strong argument for 2E</b> if it means learning 1E rules.<br /> <br /> * Bailey theirself said that the power and cost metrics were shifted mid-way through 1E development when dev leadership changed hands, making half of the 1E books designed with shifted goal posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>uh, so, getting back to what you actually said, it is pretty clear that Requiem as a whole - fluff and power - changed around the time Requiem for Rome came out (which I think is when Rose took over as dev so yeah) and I always saw 2e/Blood and Smoke as a solidification and summary of Rose-era Requiem, which, imo, makes it a better and more complete game than the entirety of 1e, which was always sort of waffling between &quot;this is Masquerade but better guys&quot; original intent and Rose-era Requiem.<br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of the Great Dev Shift halfway through Requiem. I think it's fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T11:22:48-07:00","id":1076596,"title":"","content":"One thing that hasn't been discussed all that much is that a lot of the changes that got kicked off late during Will's run were always intended to flow smoothly into a second edition. It's just that with publishing realities being what they were, the core book for that edition ended up coming out five years after the supplements started. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I even wrote some of the final VtR2 starting in 2007, just before the clanbooks.<br /> <br /> (Also, yeah, I'm a lady! Pls to not be making that the subject of an edition war.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T15:23:53-07:00","id":1076676,"title":"","content":"Obviously, first edition has a lot of books. If you want to run a first edition game, you have or have access to every book there is, detailing bloodlines, vampires in other countries, books for each covenant and clan and pre-made adventures and alternative rule sets.<br /> <br /> If you're comfortable playing a more simple game without many bloodlines and stuff, or can homebrew conversions and expansions on the fly or like using the forums for that, then second edition is a plus but not everyone is good with that.<br /> <br /> Also some people may be used to the first edition rules, some people for one reason or another don't like learning new rules or see changes to the setting as so off-putting they refuse to play it, in which case first edition is still available to them, selling on DriveThruRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-11-2017, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T17:07:35-07:00","id":1076713,"title":"","content":"Count me down as one of those who feel 2e is pretty much a straight improvement. If I were to run 1e, I'd definitely port disciplines, at least. They're just so much better.<br /> <br /> That being said, sometimes you just don't have the books, can't afford them, or don't have the time or inclination to learn new rules. Still, absent all of those, I'd pick 2e every day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:12:04-07:00","id":1076952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1075477#post1075477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You only needed two books for first edition. You currently need four books (one of them technically being 1st edition) if you want to maintain a semblance of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused by this, you only need one book for VtR:2E, you don't need the new blue core or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:38:02-07:00","id":1077028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1076952#post1076952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused by this, you only need one book for VtR:2E, you don't need the new blue core or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The keyword there is &quot;balance&quot;. Tsusai believes that in order to keep 2e Requiem &quot;balanced&quot;, you need 4 books (I'm guessing Requiem, Secrets of the Covenants, Chronicles of Darkness, Hurt Locker, and Blood Sorcery).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T11:18:53-07:00","id":1077084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077028#post1077028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The keyword there is &quot;balance&quot;. Tsusai believes that in order to keep 2e Requiem &quot;balanced&quot;, you need 4 books (I'm guessing Requiem, Secrets of the Covenants, Chronicles of Darkness, Hurt Locker, and Blood Sorcery).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably right, I'd be interested to hear how the core isn't balanced though, I've never had a problem with it. Tsusai, is the imbalance in the combat abilities or something else (relative social power of Covenants)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:44:17-07:00","id":1077443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077028#post1077028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The keyword there is &quot;balance&quot;. Tsusai believes that in order to keep 2e Requiem &quot;balanced&quot;, you need 4 books (I'm guessing Requiem, Secrets of the Covenants, Chronicles of Darkness, Hurt Locker, and Blood Sorcery).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats 5. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T21:07:45-07:00","id":1077494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077084#post1077084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're probably right, I'd be interested to hear how the core isn't balanced though, I've never had a problem with it. Tsusai, is the imbalance in the combat abilities or something else (relative social power of Covenants)</div> </div> </div> </div>Balance doesn't exist in second edition unless everyone plays the same clan and covenant or you house rule the crap out of clan signature disciplines. And that goes by the wayside if you bring in other templates.<br /> You need Blood and Smoke, God Machine Chronicle, and Sacraments and Blasphemies just for default mechanics. Otherwise you have one magic covenant with spells that do pretty much everything, one magic covenant that has some halfway decent retaliatory effects, a third magic covenant with jacked up magical powers that amplify or dispel vampiric baseline powers, the fourth covenant has some negligible parlor tricks to amuse the other three, and the fifth covenant who's purpose is to undermine and debunk the fourth covenant's tricks with their own stunts at every opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T22:12:55-07:00","id":1077528,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, I have <i>never </i>had issue keeping games balanced with 2e core alone. I only recently got Sacraments and Blasphemies and I'm not too into it, honestly.<br /> <br /> On the <i>other </i>hand, my players don't even read the books and don't pay attention to crunch or make builds, they just make characters they like, so maybe if I had more build-y crunchy players, it would be more obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T00:28:24-07:00","id":1077553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077494#post1077494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Balance doesn't exist in second edition unless everyone plays the same clan and covenant or you house rule the crap out of clan signature disciplines. And that goes by the wayside if you bring in other templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't think there should be balance between the templates, they're not classes like in D&amp;D, they're seperate games with seperate themes. A new demon should be more powerful on average than a vampire for example, I'd find the reverse to be slightly world breaking (and theme breaking in some cases) for the sake of team combat.<br /> I could be wrong though, if you feel there is a deeper problem in the rules here.<br /> <br /> Which signature disciplines are unbalanced in your view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":".  Spelling 04-13-2017, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:25:28-07:00","id":1077584,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you need 2e core for a few rules. It's nowhere near as blatant as 1e where the basic rules were only explained in the core book, but there are things that are referenced in Vampire 2e that can't be found in the book, like the foot and car chasing mechanics.<br /> <br /> And yeah, for the templates, while it seems they tried to have some balance in 1e (werewolves were pretty nerfed, to the dismay of at least on person I know), well except for the mages, 2e forgets about that, and I don't have much of a problem with it, it's like comparing apples and oranges. Mixed games have always brought a number of problems besides simple balance anyway, so if you're going to do one, you should be ready to manage a lot of things. Inside of vampire, though I find the disciplines more balanced than before (with celerity finally worth something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T03:55:42-07:00","id":1077619,"title":"","content":"An anecdote: I've mostly just skimmed Blood Sorcery so it's not my personal opinion, but before I joined my current group they had excised those rules because they made LeS and CotC way too powerful.<br /> So it kinda highlights how subjective balance is in these kinds of games where some people think one optional set of rules is so important you can't play without them, and others refuse to play with them.<br /> <br /> I personally think VtR 2E can be played with only the VtR 2E core book with no problem or having to feel like anything's missing. CofD does have a list of Merits that didn't fit in VtR due to word count that is very interesting (plus a few optional subsystems but only the social system would be central to Vampire, if it wasn't seemingly completely ignored by a majority of the players), but that makes CofD more like a source book than a second required core book like in 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-13-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T05:55:22-07:00","id":1077665,"title":"","content":"As a mid 90s V:tM player who came on board with V:tR at launch, to which I own (or owned at one point) all the books... V:tR2 is just a much better game, IMO.<br /> <br /> I really couldn't care less about &quot;balance&quot; of powers, in single-splat games (actually I could care even less, in cross-splat games). As if there is an objective way to &quot;balance&quot; super strength against mind control. It is really up to all the people involved to decide that the game should be fun for everyone and play with that in mind.<br /> <br /> So, are there valid reasons to play 1e? Yes. And just as many to play 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 04-13-2017, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:41:49-07:00","id":1077929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077584#post1077584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yeah, for the templates, while it seems they tried to have some balance in 1e (werewolves were pretty nerfed, to the dismay of at least on person I know),</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves were nerfed compared to what? 1e was the first edition, there's no previous version for them to have been nerfed from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:48:37-07:00","id":1077937,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing they're comparing it to Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:15:14-07:00","id":1078006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077937#post1077937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing they're comparing it to Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was my guess as well. I guess I should just be straightforward and <i>say</i> that treating CofD like a new edition of WoD is a pet peeve of mine instead of being passive-aggressive about it. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:57:54-07:00","id":1078023,"title":"","content":"<i>Everyone</i> in CofD (except maybe Mages) is nerfed compared to WoD because they are trying to do different things. WoD has more of an &quot;epic&quot; scope, with lore beyond lore and names and personalities and clashes of titans. CofD is more individual, personal, and, for lack of a better word, <i>realistic. </i>(I say lack of a better word because it is unproven that vampires and werewolves exist outside of fiction.)<br /> <br /> ...the only exception, again, being Mage, where you're still all-powerful and world destroying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T19:44:14-07:00","id":1078121,"title":"","content":"On the occasions when I run Requiem these days it tends to be something like Requiem 1.75<br /> <br /> I like 2E, but I only have it in PDF while I have two physical copies of 1E Requiem core. This makes 1E much easier to run at a table, particularly for players who tend to not be as familiar with Requiem as other games, but I can then incorporate as much material from later supplements and 2E as the system can reasonably accommodate while still being legible to the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T01:34:15-07:00","id":1078221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078121#post1078121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the occasions when I run Requiem these days it tends to be something like Requiem 1.75<br /> <br /> I like 2E, but I only have it in PDF while I have two physical copies of 1E Requiem core. This makes 1E much easier to run at a table, particularly for players who tend to not be as familiar with Requiem as other games, but I can then incorporate as much material from later supplements and 2E as the system can reasonably accommodate while still being legible to the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I find PDF easier to handle for a fast consultation of the rules. You can use tools as &quot;find&quot; or click on the ipertextual Index.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:52:55-07:00","id":1078383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078006#post1078006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I should just be straightforward and <i>say</i> that treating CofD like a new edition of WoD is a pet peeve of mine</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was Apocalypse, and I understand the annoyance at the type of gamers who complain about how the NewWoD isn't like the OldWod, but I really wasn't saying that. Saying that werewolves wer nerfed between the two games is not a judgement on the quality of those games in this case (unless it's part of the connotation of the expression, but well). It is a judgement when it comes from said player who, at the table, liked to remind the GM and I (neither of us played Apocalypse) that Werewolves used to be so much better at fighting and had incredible regeneration and could hold crinos indefinitely, etc. That's what he gets for being older and nostalgic.<br /> <br /> I don't really mind those changes (especially in the case of Werewolf since, while interesting, I'm more into Vampire anyway) and that was just pointing out something for the sake of argument, not a way of saying non-nerfed werewolves were better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:11:56-07:00","id":1078458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078383#post1078383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that was Apocalypse, and I understand the annoyance at the type of gamers who complain about how the NewWoD isn't like the OldWod, but I really wasn't saying that. Saying that werewolves wer nerfed between the two games is not a judgement on the quality of those games in this case (unless it's part of the connotation of the expression, but well). It is a judgement when it comes from said player who, at the table, liked to remind the GM and I (neither of us played Apocalypse) that Werewolves used to be so much better at fighting and had incredible regeneration and could hold crinos indefinitely, etc. That's what he gets for being older and nostalgic.<br /> <br /> I don't really mind those changes (especially in the case of Werewolf since, while interesting, I'm more into Vampire anyway) and that was just pointing out something for the sake of argument, not a way of saying non-nerfed werewolves were better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's just framing those differences between WoD and CofD as &quot;changes&quot; when there is no continuity between them that bothers me. It's like saying that, I dunno, vampires in True Blood are changed from Bram Stoker's Dracula. They're both about vampires, and vampires are different in each, but we don't talk about it as a change from one to the other, since they're entirely different fictional universes with no continuity from one to the other.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I get why it's often seen that way - CofD <i>was</i> originally going to replace WoD, so the changes from WoD revised to CofD 1e are kind of comparable to the changes from D&amp;D 3.X to D&amp;D 4e. It still bugs me now that they're billed as different games existing in parallel though. Most folks don't complain that wizards got nerfed from Pathfinder to D&amp;D 5e, because we all recognize that they're different games. I think WoD and CofD should be treated the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T14:21:40-07:00","id":1078531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078221#post1078221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I find PDF easier to handle for a fast consultation of the rules. You can use tools as &quot;find&quot; or click on the ipertextual Index.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely makes quick references more streamlined, but I've tended to find physical books are still better for in-person chargen and for new players in particular. Easier to move back and forth between sections, easier to remember where you &quot;are&quot; in the book, easier to share the text around the table, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T22:50:39-07:00","id":1078774,"title":"","content":"The only thing I favor in 1e is the freedom to swap Humanity for EXP during the character creation phase, which I find bothersome in 2e especially when I want to play characters who did atrocious things in their mortal background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","user":"Shawarbaaz","date":". 04-15-2017, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T03:29:35-07:00","id":1078817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078774#post1078774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing I favor in 1e is the freedom to swamp Humanity for EXP during the character creation phase, which I find bothersome in 2e especially when I want to play characters who did atrocious things in their mortal background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup you're right I like the rule also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T12:14:25-07:00","id":1078998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078458#post1078458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's just framing those differences between WoD and CofD as &quot;changes&quot; when there is no continuity between them that bothers me. It's like saying that, I dunno, vampires in True Blood are changed from Bram Stoker's Dracula. They're both about vampires, and vampires are different in each, but we don't talk about it as a change from one to the other, since they're entirely different fictional universes with no continuity from one to the other.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I get why it's often seen that way - CofD <i>was</i> originally going to replace WoD, so the changes from WoD revised to CofD 1e are kind of comparable to the changes from D&amp;D 3.X to D&amp;D 4e. It still bugs me now that they're billed as different games existing in parallel though. Most folks don't complain that wizards got nerfed from Pathfinder to D&amp;D 5e, because we all recognize that they're different games. I think WoD and CofD should be treated the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one way to see it. To me, the similarities are way too important to see the oWoD and nWod (or CoD, but the 1e books are still labelled New WoD, so to me CoD is only 2e) as completely different games, and when 2e got released, most people I talked to about Vampire the Requiem Second Edition thought I was talking about Requiem, since to them, Requiem was the second edition of Masquerade. In many ways, the nWoD directly built on oWod elements. Vampire is the most ovious example where three clans out of 5 are direct editorial descendants of the oWoD clans, and many of the other clans and bloodlines were directly inspired by Masquerade elements. Werewolf is more subtle about it, true so it's less comparable, but you can also clearly see the parallels (Blood Talons/Red Talons, Storm Lords/Get of Fenris/Silver Fangs) and I don't see how it's a problem to talk about &quot;changes&quot; between the games since there's a direct filliation (in themes, vocabulary, system). Its not like comparing the Dracula Novel to True Blood since hundreds of works about vampire and Dracula separate those two.<br /> <br /> I mean I see your point, and it's certainly more relevant to compare 1e and 2e than to compare Masquerade and Requiem , but I don't really see the problem here. There are games of the line like Changeling that, besides some superficial elements, are absolutely different games, I would never talk about individual changes between the two games, except maybe to say that they changed the game itself, but if I take vampire ? Ok, background is different, although many, many names are reminiscent, but disciplines, the idea of vampires being organized in cities (Masquerade had larger politics, but that came a bit later when the metaplot grew), blood bonds... Yeah. You can argue that they are different games, but you can also argue there are strong and direct ties between them. If it's an editorial reason, to make Requiem stand out more and not be in Masquerade's shadow (which a number of Masquerade fans would prefer), that's another thing, though, and I can understand that, but you can only go so far when you remake the clan of autocratic snobs and still call them Ventrues.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't play D&amp;D, but I'm pretty sure lots of people go on about the various changes from the different editions, I mean, this is gaming, complaining about stuff is part of the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T18:14:37-07:00","id":1079140,"title":"","content":"When D&amp;D comes out with a new edition of the game the approach is to reinvent the game. The ST system did that with the old and new Worlds of Darkness. All the editions after that shift are revisionist in nature. Lots of games create new editions by revising the current edition. A revision can be significant enough to be considered unique.<br /> <br /> Spanish, French, and Italian are all derived from local dialects of Latin. They became separate languages long ago. Italian spoken in Northern Italy is different enough from the Italian spoken in Southern Italy that sometimes Italians can't understand Italian. On the other hand, British English and American English are not distinct enough to have any real issues. Somebody might say something odd every now and then.<br /> <br /> Romance Languages. Italian. English. Reinvention. Revision. Edition Revised or N.X Edition. It is possible to complain about any changes but comparisons begin to fall apart the more extensive the changes become. Since the COD editions are progressive revisions in nature, you would not find much more than an odd rule or two to go backwards if you already are at 2e. Going backwards would be the accurate way to describe switching from 2e to 1e. Going from Requiem to Masquerade is sideways. Feel free to pick the lane of your choice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T20:34:58-07:00","id":1079660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078998#post1078998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's one way to see it. To me, the similarities are way too important to see the oWoD and nWod (or CoD, but the 1e books are still labelled New WoD, so to me CoD is only 2e) as completely different games, and when 2e got released, most people I talked to about Vampire the Requiem Second Edition thought I was talking about Requiem, since to them, Requiem was the second edition of Masquerade. In many ways, the nWoD directly built on oWod elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>While both games have grown apart from each other this part still holds true, having recently gotten to re-read masquerade is like all roads lead to masquerade in many design choices that still carry from them, specially those plain just dont work with the current games.<br /> <br /> Yes both games are different but reading OWoD and NWoD/Chrod is an interesting though exercise as you can see many of the hows and whys of many things almost in a anthropological way. If you see something that dont quite work in requiem, forsaken or mage chances are is a holdout from the previous edition that works quite well-ish there but just feels odd in the NWOD.<br /> <br /> Egregious examples that come up in my mind are:<br /> <br /> Gargoyles from Requiem whose name makes little sense for what are and should have being name &quot;golems&quot; but instead they got an ill fitted name for their Masquerade counter parts.<br /> <br /> Forsaken has the term gifts that even the line has a section in Lore of the forsaken explaining how that name makes no sense in the context of Forsaken.<br /> <br /> And where characters start in chargen from all games that only truly made sense in Masquerade but was used and re-used in all lines to the detriment of all of them.<br /> <br /> Yes they are different lines/games with both pros and cons but the comparison would still be made because they are similar games made by follow up companies and sometimes even the developers continue that line of thinking.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077929#post1077929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves were nerfed compared to what? 1e was the first edition, there's no previous version for them to have been nerfed from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue they were nerfed compared to their own fluff in 1E. Like the authors had Apocalypse power level in their heads when writing the fiction.<br /> <br /> As for the 1st edition vs 2nd, as others have point out there is the issue of 1st edition having more books that require no conversion while second does need a little, not much mind you but it does have a problem.<br /> <br /> Also 2nd in general has a certain power creep in their splats which some people might have problems with and others dont. But 1st edition vampire were much weaker at the start than their 2nd edition counterparts. And a well made human could stand a chance against them one on one to a certain level.<br /> <br /> And finally is the issue of freedom vs vision. 2nd edition mechanics gear towards A style of play while 1st edition have a bunch of mechanics that clumsily carry the game with little to no synergy between them. The latter makes ignoring certain mechanics for an alternative style of play easier while 2nd edition\u00b4s mechanics interface with its themes which at the same time makes it difficult to play it when you wanna play vampire but dont quite buy into those themes.<br /> <br /> Example 2nd puts lots of mechanical emphasis in Vampires dealing with their human lives, some people like to play that. Others like to play characters completely immersed in their supernatural lives without it being a &quot;thing&quot; as dealing with human life, friends or family is boring to them or their foregone conclusion is not something they care about. 2nd edition lets you play that character but it makes it a &quot;thing&quot; with consequences while in 1st it didnt.<br /> <br /> So someone that would like to play a vampire, like the setting but dont necessarily buy into 2nd edition themes could choose 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 04-17-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:20:54-07:00","id":1079825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1078998#post1078998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and when 2e got released, most people I talked to about Vampire the Requiem Second Edition thought I was talking about Requiem, since to them, Requiem was the second edition of Masquerade. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to say, that doesn't make much sense since there were three editions of Masquerade before Requiem even came out. The point being that people who ignore editions of a game are not the most reliable source for how new games that are spiritual successors should be treated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T01:46:21-07:00","id":1080219,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but the fact that this was their general feeling tells me something about how different a game NWoD and OWoD are perceived. What i'm saying is it seems to be more a semantics thing, really, and not a particularly important one at that. I mean, maybe this is an exactly science, to say what is and isn't a totally different game but somehow, I don't think it is. Mostly, though, if we call it a different game, you gotta admit it's a hell of a weird case. 1e is kinda of a strange buffer zone for a lot of things between Masquerade and 2e, there are all those terms that got brought over, groups that were directly inspired by Masquerade (maybe one of the reasons Belial's Brood hasn't appeared yet in 2e is so people don't see it and go &quot;oh, so that's what the Sabbat/Baali look like now ?&quot;). To me, yes, both games are two different to be called the same (since editions of each brought fewer changes and the transition from Masquerade to Requiem), but to say you can't talk about changes between the games, that they're completely different ? I don't follow that. Not when Requiem 1e brought back Nosferatu except it said &quot;but our Nosferatu are different, they're not all physically ugly, and they have a new unique discipline&quot;, or &quot;So there's the Malkovians, with an &quot;O&quot;, don't forget that important detail, they're crazy because people loves Malkavians from Masquerade, but they're not the same (and they suck, so just wait until the Ventrue book to have something actually fun where it's going to be a blood sickness called Malkavia)&quot;, or &quot;So here are the Khaibit, they use shadows, because manipulating shadows is cool since the Lassombra did that too and people dug them, but now, they're just a bloodline and their seemingly useless powers may or may not give them way to fight the strix from that other supplement, although we're never gonna confirm that&quot;. And I'm making fun or 1e like that, but don't misunderstand. I love that game. I wouldn't have GM'd it twice (once for 3 years, and once for 1 year and a half) if I didn't, but it's a clusterfuck and pretty much the RPG equivalent of a tsundere in it's relationship to Masquerade. And you know what ? That's okay, I don't mind that. It was the first game of the new line, it ddidn't really know what it wanted to be so it shot in all directions until something stuck, and it played on the Masquerade nostalgia to tell players &quot;See, we're the new Vampire, but don't worry, you can still play a Ventrue and be and asshole, and it'll be just like old time&quot;. Hell, it took a while until the Night Horrors : The Wicked Dead came out and provided a major splat antagonist that was strong enough to stand on its own without having to reference Masquerade.<br /> <br /> And again, it's completely fine. They wanted to make the line more of a toolkit to make your own game and I have to say they succeeded at that (only problem is when you have that many tools, it's hard to have them all and it's easy to be confused, but that's part of gaming). A good game isn't necessarily a neatly self contained game with no loose ends that has to be perfectly defined in a single book (although money-wise, that last part is always appreciable), it's a game you can have fun with. And you could have a LOT of fun with 1e, but the lineage with Masquerade ? It's there, it's part of it's identity and I don't think it's wrong to point it out and comment on how some of the many elements that appear in both games were adapted or, yes, changed<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said, the argument I could understand is if the people who made/published the game WANT it to be labelled a different game because it makes things unclear otherwise and because, in this particular case, there seem to be a weird silent war between the newer editions of OWoD (now called &quot;Classic&quot; WoD I guess) and NWoD/CWoD (although Onyx Path owns both).<br /> <br /> I should also note that I'm puzzled as to why Classic WoD is seeing new editions yet. I thought Time of Judgement was a way to close that game once and for all. I thought 20th anniversary was just a way to issue a neat book that compiled all the important information of the previous books, but I guess that was a new edition altogether, and I don't really see the point (well, that's not true, I can guess fans asked for it, there was profit to be made and so it was made, because rpg publishing houses don't exactly fund themselves). It's still super weird to have these two games hanging around at the same time, like two alternate reality versions of the same person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:21:10-07:00","id":1080331,"title":"","content":"Oh for sure, it is fine to say that they are related games, or as has been said a 'spiritual successor'. No one is denying that.<br /> <br /> Personally, I was just saying that people who call Requiem the second edition of Masquerade are not the people who would really now since they don't seem to know that there were those other editions (by that logic, Requiem would be the 4th edition of Vampire, not the second). That tells me that the only they they count as a new edition IS the nomenclature and large-scale rules changes despite that not being the case as far as the publisher and owner are concerned.<br /> <br /> To your last points, a few clarifications. Both World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness are owned by White Wolf Publishing not Onyx Path. Onyx Path has the license to create table top games based on them. World of Darkness was called Classic while the 20th Anniversary editions were coming out because it was no longer 'old', it was current. White Wolf wants to push it because it is a larger, more well known property and we will likely see more and more things with that name, while it seems Chronicles will, for the moment at least, stay a tabletop only product.<br /> <br /> This actually lends further evidence to the idea that Requiem should not be seen as an edition of Masquerade, since they will both be coming out concurrently without any connections at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:56:31-07:00","id":1080954,"title":"","content":"And like... to be fair, a lot of this is pretty obscure behind-the-scenes knowledge that the average fan wouldn't have cause to know. And even for those who are interested the language can be downright obfuscating. White Wolf Publishing, Crowd Control Productions, Onyx Path Publishing, Paradox Interactive, White Wolf Publishing again, (old) World of Darkness, (new) World of Darkness, Classic World of Darkness, (new) World of Darkness Second Edition, (one) World of Darkness Chronicles of Darkness, and what the heck is a &quot;Chronicle Book&quot; anyway? Unfortunately, the whole thing is doomed to be confusing as hell for ever. Still, treating the intellectual property formerly known as World of Darkness, currently known as Chronicles of Darkness as an edition of the intellectual property formerly known as World of Darkness, then as Classic World of Darkness, and now known as World of Darkness again is still a pet peeve for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-19-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:59:25-07:00","id":1080957,"title":"","content":"Oh certainly, I think that the last points about companies and rights and such is a confusing mess that is really a separate issue from whether or not people identify the editions of either game set correctly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T05:33:57-07:00","id":1081399,"title":"","content":"I don't think the legal aspect is a completely separate issue from what the readers perceive. There's probably a lot to get from that info about what was intended in given game and how that intent either got fulfilled or changed through editorial shenanigans.<br /> <br /> About the people I talked to and made the comment about OWoD being the old edition, they knew the game pretty well and are much more familiar with it than I am. It's still possible they didn't identify various editions to Masquerade, but it's also possible they used the term &quot;edition&quot; loosely (which i don't really have a problem about).<br /> <br /> How the OWoD got brought back and became CWoD certainly makes it more confusing. I mean, ok, 2e and the, now, Chronicles of Darkness are decidedly trying to be independent from the OWoD, but then you have Requiem 1e that really felt, at the time, like the continuation of Masquerade except changed since the OWoD had blown up (one way or another) with a new identity. Then 20th anniversary edition comes up like a resurrected Jason Todd and it's all starting anew. Seems to me Requiem was retroactively put in the position of a branching entity, rather than a successor. Now, yes, compared to 20th Anniversary Edition, Requiem (even 1e, but especially 2e) is absolutely a different game since they both coexist develop separately, but I don't see how that cancels out how Requiem 1e was basically made from the ashes of Masquerade (also with the lessons from other games like exhalted too I guess) as its &quot;sequel&quot; after Gehenna (and Time of Judgement in general) officially ended the old line.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of this has to do with what you can and cannot (or decide you can and cannot) call an &quot;edition&quot;, and really, I don't know. We talk about editions of D&amp;D, which Rose described as different games (and of course, there is D&amp;D and AD&amp;D, D&amp;D3 and Pathfinder), but then you have games were editions only describe minor changes and you can still use old books for a bunch of things. So what constitutes a game from a edition ? Publisher intent ? Book compatibility ? The way I see it, a little bit of both, but in the end, it's what you're willing to call an edition, not something written in stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T06:45:16-07:00","id":1081418,"title":"","content":"So, after all of that, we're right back to &quot;I get why they're often seen that way, since CofD 1e was originally written to replace WoD, but it still bugs me that people continue to treat it that way now that they're billed as two separate entities.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T19:03:30-07:00","id":1081660,"title":"","content":"I understand confusion. I don't get comparing apples to oranges. Any two things can be compared and contrasted. Going back to the origin of this mess, in this section of the forums saying Werewolves were nerfed means in Forsaken 2e Werewolves were nerfed compared to 1e unless another context is provided. I mean if I had started going on about how wrong this nerfing suggestion is because in D&amp;D werewolves were much weaker in response to the question, people would think I was mental. D&amp;D woofs came before Apocalypse woofs. You might say but they are completely different games. Yeah, so are Apocalypse and Forsaken. I don't know what to say to someone that wouldn't see that. The name thing doesn't give it away?<br /> <br /> Apples to oranges all the way. Before we go down that road, tell me we are comparing fruit first or provide another appropriate context. Otherwise, I don't understand. The apple has a reddish color, with a smooth, thin not very orange-like peel. The shape is...well, the shape is like an apple because it is an apple and not an orange so this whole comparison is moronic. Comparing an apple as if it was an orange is where people start to walk.<br /> <br /> Keep it clear. nWoD and oWoD are two separate game lines and not versions of the same thing even when referencing similar supers. Talking about them as if they were the same is incorrect. I'm not objecting to the comparisons, but I will roll my eyes when people try to say Requiem is a version of Masquerade. I think the timeline would be something like Masquerade, Revised Masquerade, Masquerade (mine has no edition stated other than the print), Requiem, V20, Requiem 2, then whatever the new WW is coming out with. I have an easier time keeping track over who owns the license than that garbage timeline. Masquerade was dead when Requiem appeared. Somebody dug Masquerade back up and the rest of the oWoD with it. Plenty of confusion with all the different names but it isn't difficult to keep different games straight.<br /> <br /> Requiem 1 is a transition between Masquerade and Requiem 2 in the same way Masquerade is a transition between D&amp;D and Requiem. The transition covers less between Masquerade and Requiem. There is the big difference between the two comparisons. They are all different games.<br /> <br /> Reason for Rant: People that say something like Requiem is a later version of Masquerade don't know what they are talking about so are unreliable sources about WoD games. Maybe they are right about other things, but they sure got that one wrong. If someone can't tell the difference between an apple and an orange, don't trust them to buy your fruit. That's all I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 04-20-2017, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T21:00:52-07:00","id":1081691,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, comparing apples to oranges is something that a lot of us Requiem STs have to do. There are a lot of people who remember Masquerade very fondly(and often, distantly), who can be mistrustful of Requiem for all the stock reasons. If somebody looks at Requiem and notes sourly that it looks a whole lot like Masquerade, you can't tell them that Requiem is as different from Masquerade as it is from D&amp;D, because that is clearly not the case. You have to learn how to compare their apples to your oranges, and to continue the metaphor, you've got to be able to explain (in a favorable way, this is important) why that orange tastes so appley.<br /> <br /> Often, it's just a matter of breaking down negative hype. Most of my Vampire table is made up of former Masquerade LARPers, almost none of whom arrived at the table with postive preconceptions of Requiem until experiencing it firsthand and thus being able to appreciate it objectively, without the knee-jerk reaction that many of us have come to expect. Today, my players all very happy with the state of Requiem 2E and looking forward to more, but not all of us would have been if I hadn't been able to translate fruits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T21:59:35-07:00","id":1081706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081691#post1081691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to learn how to compare their apples to your oranges, and to continue the metaphor, you've got to be able to explain (in a favorable way, this is important) why that orange tastes so appley.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I've had much more success explaining why oranges don't have to be appley to be good. If what you want is an apple, an apple will always be more satisfying than an orange will be, so convincing someone who wants an apple that an orange is like an apple will only ever convince them that oranges aren't as bad as they thought. Convincing them that oranges are good in their own right, and that their similar taste to apples is just an artifact of both containing fructose will be far more effective at getting them to actually eat and enjoy oranges sometimes.<br /> <br /> And that, in a nutshell (or maybe in an orange peel?) is exactly why treating CofD as an edition of WoD is a pet peeve for me. It's counter-productive to getting WoD fans to appreciate CofD for what it is, instead of accepting it in spite of what it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T23:19:51-07:00","id":1081723,"title":"","content":"Neither of you are actually comparing apples to oranges as the metaphor suggests. You maintain that an apple is an apple which is a distinct fruit from an orange. If it is Masquerade and Requiem then it would be more like a grapefruit to an orange, but it isn't really too important which fruit we use. They are always distinct things and any comparison assumes that. If you buy a bag of oranges and try to compare the oranges to each other, you really hope someone didn't slip in a few apples. Requiem was written in Masquerade terms, if you will, at the beginning. WW was recreating Vampire so Masquerade was the starting point for a new game. Lots of similarities and points of comparison exist. Requiem 2 is a new version of Requiem created with the first edition as the starting point. Nothing in any version of Masquerade is relevant to changes in Requiem.<br /> <br /> Conflating Masquerade and Requiem brings to mind statements like the Camarilla is really weak and disorganized in Requiem. Really? I imagine it would be since it ceased to exist in Requiem hundreds of years ago. The Invictus is not the Camarilla. The Camarilla is not even what we imagine the Masquerade's Camarilla to be. We can compare the two Camarillas, but we need to keep them separate which with the names becomes more difficult. The Invictus is irrelevant to the comparison unless we are talking about the roles they play in their respective games. Yet, we always have apples and oranges rather than oranges to oranges. The metaphor has always been to say don't compare two different things as if they were the same. <br /> <br /> Saying the Camarilla has really fallen apart in Requiem since Masquerade makes no sense, apples to oranges. Saying the Camarilla-like organization in Requiem is not the far-reaching power that is in Masquerade does, oranges to oranges.<br /> <br /> This is an old argument. All I would ask is people keep their comparisons clear, keep the terms of the comparison clear. Anyone that won't do that will have a hard time being understood. How can someone else know you mean the Invictus when you say the Camarilla? With all the overlapping terms, it is confusing enough when people don't start mixing games deliberately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T01:46:50-07:00","id":1081751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081418#post1081418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, after all of that, we're right back to &quot;I get why they're often seen that way, since CofD 1e was originally written to replace WoD, but it still bugs me that people continue to treat it that way now that they're billed as two separate entities.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Now that they're billed as two different entities. That's the thing. So now that the publishers has stated that those games are totally different, it invalidates the fact that they sold it as the replacement for Masquerade ? This is what I'm talking about here. All those ridiculous comparisons with D&amp;D (a game from a different publisher, with an independent publishing history, which is about playing in a medieval fantastic setting, with character classes, and all the things that make it entirely different from anything White Wolf has ever been doing with either the OWoD or the CoD) are a nice straw man argument, except the OWoD was never sold as the sequel to D&amp;D, which the NWoD was.<br /> <br /> Diggs' argument that &quot;They're just different games and that's it&quot; is nothing more than publisher fiat. &quot;They're different games because we say they are&quot;. Well, great, that solves the problem, but that's a perfectly arbitrary view. It's not wrong, because there's no essential truth about what a game is and what makes it different, so yes, I agree with Charlaquin on that post that it's a question of how the publisher advertised it. It used to be advertised one way, now it's advertised another way, but just because the publisher says it doesn't mean I have to see it that way since there are also very good arguments for the other view that Requiem and Masquerade are closely related and while calling them editions (in the way that 1e and 2e differ) is not quite right, calling them unrelated game is also not quite right.<br /> <br /> I don't know, but i'm very disturbed by this retroactive thing right here. It happened and it's part of the game's identity, and I'm not going to forget it just cause the publisher says so, I find that super creepy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T08:39:40-07:00","id":1081861,"title":"","content":"A replacement doesn't necessarily mean a sequel.<br /> <br /> And you know about these games, and while your posts are focusing on the similarities between them for the purpose of your argument, you are clearly aware of the differences in mood, theme, scope and scale. You've been part of the board since 2015 and while I'm not sure how often you've posted you must be aware that Requiem, Forsaken and Awakening aren't considered continuations of Masquerade, Apocalypse and Ascension by any but those who really want there to be a connection, to enjoy an extended metaplot, similar to those who try to connect movie or TV universes together.<br /> <br /> The difference between lines should be more obvious by the others. Geist, Changeling, Promethean are nothing like classic's Wraith, Changeling, and nothing, and clinging onto some idea that they must be the same, that things do not change over time, that similar terms were used for some reason beyond them being established among a desired customer-base, seems to have no purpose other than allowing you to post things like this.<br /> <br /> Simple fact is these games were always meant to be different. They have some of the same subject matter and share much terminology, or artifacts that writers in New thought players of Old would like or that the writers liked enough to warrant a new variant of. But Requiem was never Masquerade v4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T10:32:02-07:00","id":1081901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the Vampire: Requiem 1st Edition Acknowledgement</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to the visionaries who broke boundaries and redefined roleplaying with the previous incarnation of Vampire: Mark Rein\u2022Hagen, Stewart Wieck, Steven C. Brown, Tom Dowd, Andrew Greenberg, Jennifer Hartshorn, Robert Hatch, Lisa Stevens, Josh Timbrook and the unsung contributors whose names were never mentioned but who nonetheless know who they are. We couldn\u2019t have done it without the trail you blazed before us. Special thanks to you, whether you\u2019re joining us again after 13 years of thrills and chills or just showing up for the first time. Game on!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am unconvinced by the arguments that Requiem is not the spiritual successor to Masquerade. They share focus, they share themes, they share mechanics, and they share terminology. The semantic argument over 'sequel vs. replacement vs. version vs. incarnation' is splitting hairs. Every Vampire gaming table had to make a decision when Requiem came out - play in the new version, or keep playing with the now unsupported version (v20 was not on the radar). These were not the same arguments that a table would have over whether to play D&amp;D or Shadowrun.<br /> <br /> CofD is it's own thing <i>now</i> because of licensing issues and the resurrection of White Wolf after CCP. If Onyx Path had acquired the license/rights from CCP instead of Paradox would they be different things? I'm not so sure they would. Anyway, my point is you can say they are different and point out the big changes and evolutions that are still ongoing without pretending that Requiem wasn't a replacement for Masquerade. It certainly felt like and was advertised as being the successor/replacement at the time.<br /> <br /> edit: I feel as if this conversation is like people saying it isn't fair/correct to compare <i>Star Trek: Wrath of Khan</i> to <i>Star Trek: Into Darkness</i> because ST:ID isn't a sequel or replacement for ST:WoK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":". 04-21-2017, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T10:45:38-07:00","id":1081907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081901#post1081901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: I feel as if this conversation is like people saying it isn't fair/correct to compare <i>Star Trek: Wrath of Khan</i> to <i>Star Trek: Into Darkness</i> because ST:ID isn't a sequel or replacement for ST:WoK.</div> </div> </div> </div>Comparing them is entirely valid. The various Translation guides point out the differences between the games, and explains things people might prefer to see in one or the other.<br /> <br /> But are you really going to say Into Darkness is Wrath of Khan Part 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T10:57:26-07:00","id":1081915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081907#post1081907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are you really going to say Into Darkness is Wrath of Khan Part 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for the hair-splitting semantics of it not being a linear continuation of the previous Wrath of Khan movie, yes - I would in fact say that. It is the same characters, the same conflicts, the same universe - retold by a different director and creative team (writers, actors, etc).<br /> <br /> But yes, if you want me to say it isn't a direct continuation - I guess you win that one. Requiem wasn't meant as a 'direct continuation' either - i.e. After the Gehenna plotline all the characters in Masquerade didn't suddenly find themselves ported to the Requiem timeline/universe for a redo.<br /> <br /> I honestly have no idea the relevance of that argument, though, to this thread.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:06:34-07:00","id":1081917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081915#post1081915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for the hair-splitting semantics of it not being a linear continuation of the previous Wrath of Khan movie, yes - I would in fact say that. It is the same characters, the same conflicts, the same universe - retold by a different director and creative team (writers, actors, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think Requiem and Masquerade share the same conflicts, universe and characters? The World of Darkness itself is different between classic, where the focus was on the evil horrors of the world, and new, which shifts the topic down to the common person and the darkness is representative of mystery, not evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, if you want me to say it isn't a direct continuation - I guess you win that one. Requiem wasn't meant as a 'direct continuation' either - i.e. After the Gehenna plotline all the characters in Masquerade didn't suddenly find themselves ported to the Requiem timeline/universe for a redo. </div> </div> </div>S. Brechen's argument is that these games are direct continuations and that them being 'different games' is a falsehood, and some sort of spin on behalf of the publisher that attempts to cover that up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I honestly have no idea the relevance of that argument, though, to this thread. </div> </div> </div>The thread has derailed from its original topic into arguing over S. Brechen's views of what is and is not different between editions. The original topic was 'is there any reason to play first edition over second, other than nostalgia.'<br /> <br /> This is all off topic from that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-21-2017, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:10:07-07:00","id":1081919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081907#post1081907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Comparing them is entirely valid. The various Translation guides point out the differences between the games, and explains things people might prefer to see in one or the other.<br /> <br /> But are you really going to say Into Darkness is Wrath of Khan Part 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call it a sequel but I would say to anyone trying to claim Into Darkness wasn't a half assed rip off to the Wrath of Khan that they're ignorant.<br /> <br /> If they wanted to differentiate themselves from the original Star Trek movie and television series, then they should have told a different story. Instead they decided to rip off the plot and dialogue wholesale of the single best Star Trek movie in the entire movie line up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:12:44-07:00","id":1081921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081917#post1081917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think Requiem and Masquerade share the same conflicts, universe and characters? The World of Darkness itself is different between classic, where the focus was on the evil horrors of the world, and new, which shifts the topic down to the common person and the darkness is representative of mystery, not evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying they <i>don't</i> share conflict, setting and character features? It's pretty clear to me they do, even when some of them have evolved and changed. And don't get me wrong, I like those evolutions. It takes me a bit to adjust my mindset to play Masquerade as I feel like it's going backwards. And that's not meant as a dig to anyone who prefers Masquerade over Requiem, people should use the tools they enjoy most. So I don't think anyone is denying real differences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081917#post1081917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S. Brechen's argument is that these games are direct continuations and that them being 'different games' is a falsehood, and some sort of spin on behalf of the publisher that attempts to cover that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they? I think it's possible to both recognize that Masquerade &amp; Requiem don't share IC-continuity, while also being able to recognize they are continuations as a game line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:36:46-07:00","id":1081934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081921#post1081921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying they <i>don't</i> share conflict, setting and character features? It's pretty clear to me they do, even when some of them have evolved and changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masquerade was focused on being thrust into the conflict between age old vendettas, summed up in the Jyhad, while Requiem is focused on the immediate concern of what to do when you're dead, the Requiem. The setting is Earth, but different. Masquerade's World of Darkness is 'the real world, but evil.' While Requiem is, 'the real world, but more mysterious.' And I obviously wouldn't say they share characters, beyond maybe Dracula, and that's more of a nod to the book than classic's version. Despite names, the clans are different, the covenants are different from the sects. Things do share similarities, but saying something like Belial's Brood is the same as the Sabbat is not understanding one or the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It takes me a bit to adjust my mindset to play Masquerade as I feel like it's going backwards. And that's not meant as a dig to anyone who prefers Masquerade over Requiem, people should use the tools they enjoy most. So I don't think anyone is denying real differences. </div> </div> </div>Someone liking one thing or another shouldn't have any bearing on this situation except to possibly take sides. But the idea of 'going backwards' seems to be a perception based on your past experience. I played Requiem first, never had to make a decision about which to play, because I wasn't interested in Masquerade. My experience could offer me a lot of arguments that, vary from yours or whoever elses, so its probably best to deal with the games as they are, rather than our own experiences with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are they? I think it's possible to both recognize that Masquerade &amp; Requiem don't share IC-continuity, while also being able to recognize they are continuations as a game line. </div> </div> </div>That's what a continuation means, though. You're carrying one thing on to the other. My life now is a continuation of my life yesterday. My child's life is not a continuation of my life, though it would be a continuation of my genetic heritage, as those genes are being carried on. If Requiem was a continuation, it would be carrying over more than the superficial aspects already noted, it would be continuing on with Gehenna, one way or another.<br /> <br /> A remake or homage, like with Wrath of Khan and Into Darkness. A spiritual successor. A new or different World of Darkness. All these things fit. Continuation doesn't beyond talking about the continuation of White Wolf publishing, or 'modern horror,' 'playing monsters,' 'storytelling games,' the major commonalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-21-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T11:52:17-07:00","id":1081944,"title":"","content":"A continuation of publishers. A continuation of concepts. Of many themes. Of many rules. Of many terms and many definitions. Some things changed, some more than others. Some things remained. The timeline did not remain.<br /> <br /> You seem able to see the above and conclude that you can't use the word 'continuation' in an accurate manner when discussing Requiem and Masquerade. I see the same words and conclude the exact opposite. Thank you for expressing your viewpoint (truly, I do like game theory discussions and I'm bored at work), but I think we're at that agree-to-disagree impasse as I don't think I'll ever see the carry-over between the two lines as simply superficial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:04:19-07:00","id":1081950,"title":"","content":"Chronicles is absolutely a spiritual successor to World. What it is not is an edition of World. I know people don't like the D&amp;D comparison, but it's more relevant than the Star Trek comparison because of conventions unique to the RPG genre. Pathfinder is a spiritual successor to D&amp;D, as is 13th age, but neither are Editions of D&amp;D. If you really want to compare to film though, The Amazing Spider-Man is not a sequel to Spider Man 3.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or better yet, video games! Overwatch is not a sequel to Team Fortress 2. It doesn't make sense to say that Heavies got nerfed or buffed from TF2 to Overwatch, because while Overwatch has tank-style heroes (I would assume), which may be stronger or weaker in Overwatch's metagame than Heavies were in TF2, they are not Editions of the same franchise, so the differences in meta game impact are not called nerfs or buffs. Likewise, while World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness both feature werewolves, it doesn't make sense to say CofD's werewolves were &quot;nerfed&quot; from WoD's werewolves because they are not Editions of the same franchise. The Forsaken are not the Garou, and differences in their &quot;power level&quot; are not nerfs or buffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-21-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:39:40-07:00","id":1081969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081950#post1081950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles is absolutely a spiritual successor to World. What it is not is an edition of World. I know people don't like the D&amp;D comparison, but it's more relevant than the Star Trek comparison because of conventions unique to the RPG genre. Pathfinder is a spiritual successor to D&amp;D, as is 13th age, but neither are Editions of D&amp;D. If you really want to compare to film though, The Amazing Spider-Man is not a sequel to Spider Man 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with your Pathfinder analogy, because that was done by a 3rd party under an open publishing license with particular requirements not to replace the original work. (I'm not familiar with 13th Age).<br /> <br /> Requiem and Masquerade are different editions of the Vampire game line. If you want to argue that they are different franchises of the line, yeah - that's true.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, you guys interested in a game of Vampire this weekend?&quot;<br /> &quot;Which edition - Masquerade, Requiem?&quot;<br /> <br /> The answer here should probably be one of the many editions of the Vampire game line (Requiem, Masquerade, End Times, v20, Dark Ages, New Wave Requiem, etc). It probably shouldn't be...<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, those are different franchises so I'm not sure it's accurate to refer to them as editions like that.&quot;<br /> <br /> It kind of breaks down for me on the common sense angle. I continue to concede the semantics angle, and add my support to the following statement being an incorrect language usage, &quot;Vampire: The Requiem is one of the editions of Vampire: The Masquerade.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1080219#post1080219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">To me, yes, both games are two different to be called the same (since editions of each brought fewer changes and the transition from Masquerade to Requiem), but to say you can't talk about changes between the games, that they're completely different ? I don't follow that.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">S. Brechen seems to be conceding that they are different games with real changes that mean they cannot be called the same thing. Others don't seem to be conceding that it's reasonable someone see them as different editions of the same base game at all.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T12:58:29-07:00","id":1081983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081950#post1081950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, while World of Darkness and Chronicles of Darkness both feature werewolves, it doesn't make sense to say CofD's werewolves were &quot;nerfed&quot; from WoD's werewolves because they are not Editions of the same franchise. The Forsaken are not the Garou, and differences in their &quot;power level&quot; are not nerfs or buffs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except from my experience this is what happened in reality and it made perfect sense. I participated in long discussions about these things when talking about switch-over between the editions. &quot;Ventrue lose Presence and gain Animalism? What a rip.&quot; These were real world legitimate conversations and I don't see how they are invalidated by the semantics of: 'Technically, they are different franchises, so we shouldn't even be comparing them.'<br /> <br /> Talking about or comparing Masquerade Nosferatu vs. Requiem Nosferatu is not the same conversation as talking about or comparing Pathfinder Elves vs. Warhammer Fantasy elves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":".  edited for tone 04-21-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T17:39:26-07:00","id":1082071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081901#post1081901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CofD is it's own thing <i>now</i> because of licensing issues and the resurrection of White Wolf after CCP. If Onyx Path had acquired the license/rights from CCP instead of Paradox would they be different things? I'm not so sure they would.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were able to make the change to Chronicles of Darkness when WWP suggested the option for the name change because we were already repositioning those game lines further from WoD than they originally were. So if we had somehow, don't ask me how, fallen into ownership of nWoD, rebranding would have been the first thing we would have explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T18:26:44-07:00","id":1082083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081969#post1081969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with your Pathfinder analogy, because that was done by a 3rd party under an open publishing license with particular requirements not to replace the original work. (I'm not familiar with 13th Age).</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, who published it is less relevant to the distinction between the games than the fact that they are set in different fictional worlds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081969#post1081969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem and Masquerade are different editions of the Vampire game line. If you want to argue that they are different franchises of the line, yeah - that's true.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Vampire game line&quot; that you refer to isn't a thing that exists. They are different game lines that are both about vampires. Granted, they share a great deal of DNA but ultimately one is a spiritual successor to another, not a direct continuation of the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081969#post1081969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hey, you guys interested in a game of Vampire this weekend?&quot;<br /> &quot;Which edition - Masquerade, Requiem?&quot;<br /> <br /> The answer here should probably be one of the many editions of the Vampire game line (Requiem, Masquerade, End Times, v20, Dark Ages, New Wave Requiem, etc). It probably shouldn't be...<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, those are different franchises so I'm not sure it's accurate to refer to them as editions like that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all, I would say &quot;Are you guys interested in a game of Requiem this weekend?&quot; to avoid that particular ambiguity, and second of all, if I did say Vampire instead of Requiem and my friend responded in that way, my response would probably be something along the lines of, &quot;Requiem. But it's a pretty different setting from Masquerade, do you need to brush up on it before we start?&quot;<br /> <br /> Hypothetically, anyway. My friends I play CofD with were introduced to it first, and most of them haven't played WoD, but that's beside the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081969#post1081969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kind of breaks down for me on the common sense angle. I continue to concede the semantics angle, and add my support to the following statement being an incorrect language usage, &quot;Vampire: The Requiem is one of the editions of Vampire: The Masquerade.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">S. Brechen seems to be conceding that they are different games with real changes that mean they cannot be called the same thing. Others don't seem to be conceding that it's reasonable someone see them as different editions of the same base game at all.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Because I don't think it is reasonable to see them of different editions of the same base game. Frankly, I don't think it's ever been reasonable, but at least there was an excuse before WoD started getting active support again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081983#post1081983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except from my experience this is what happened in reality and it made perfect sense. I participated in long discussions about these things when talking about switch-over between the editions. &quot;Ventrue lose Presence and gain Animalism? What a rip.&quot; These were real world legitimate conversations and I don't see how they are invalidated by the semantics of: 'Technically, they are different franchises, so we shouldn't even be comparing them.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I had those conversations too. I humored them then, because the people who were making those complaints had lost their game. Support for it was stopping in favor of support for my game, so I understood the frustration and the need to treat the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness like a 3rd edition that made significant setting changes. But as each gameline that came out drifted further afield of its spiritual predecessor, it became more clear that this way of looking at it was not consistent with the developers' intent. They were meant to be completely different settings, not just updates to the same one. The x20 editions and the official branding of &quot;old&quot; World of Darkness as Classic World of Darkness was for us the final nail in the coffin. They were different games, both getting active support, there was no longer any point in making these comparisons because they existed parallel to each other. When the CofD Second Editions started coming out, the differences between the two Worlds of Darkness started be celebrated rather than lamented. When the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness got re-branded as Chronicles of Darkness, we all breathed a sigh of relief, glad that they would finally be <i>called</i> different things like they should have been all along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081983#post1081983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about or comparing Masquerade Nosferatu vs. Requiem Nosferatu is not the same conversation as talking about or comparing Pathfinder Elves vs. Warhammer Fantasy elves.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it is a very similar conversation to comparing Golarion's elves (from Pathfinder) with Faerun's elves (from D&amp;D). They share the same name, and the settings share a lot of tropes, but they do not have continuity between them, so it's weird to talk about &quot;nerfs&quot; or &quot;buffs&quot; between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T19:42:19-07:00","id":1082099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jin Keota</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire#post1075440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now here is my conundrum.<br /> <br /> I have been a collector of nWoD (CoD now) all my RPGing days, the largest part of the collection has always been VtR. Despite this and my love for the material I never got an opportunity to run or play in a VtR game, it has always been either straight up blue book games or HtV. So those books have been sitting on the shelf, read but never played.<br /> <br /> Now however I've got a group that is finally interested in playing Vampires and I'm at a crossroads. I've been running the 2nd edition CoD rules for the last few years and have the VtR 2nd edition ruleset. I've been loving changes to the core system but I feel a longing to play the 1st edition ones and use them at least once.<br /> <br /> In the end I'll probably just run the 2nd edition rules, as this group are used to the CoD system, but I'm interested in hearing from those who have run and played both version.<br /> <br /> In your opinion, are they any reasons to play 1st edition over 2nd edition beyond simple nostalgia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Considering I bought the 1E book and didn't find out until later it was outdated, I too would like an answer to this! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1075477#post1075477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I get the feeling this is a loaded question fishing for an edition war, I'll answer. Yes, there are many reasons to play 1st edition over 2nd edition. It's called personal preference, not nostalgia. Developer bias started creeping in the 1st edition publishings but it is blatant and in your face with 2nd edition. I don't like their &quot;fixes&quot; to the things I considered a problem or could see how/why others considered it a problem. And in fact, they ended up making those problems worse. The power disparity between clans and covenants is wider now to where I can't suspend disbelief. I had to make changes to a lot of the mechanics and ideology. There's also default themes and elements. 2nd ed. is a lot more about rapidly plunging down a nihilistic spiral of self destruction and gaining as much instant temporary gratification along the way. Whereas 1st edition is more about slowly moving toward that end but trying to avoid it while amassing power. I personally liked spending over 8 years of real life gaming time rising from city hound to city regent as did the others I gamed with who moved to similar positions of power but I also realize most people today don't have that kind of attention span. Powers that wear off at the next sunset or get pulled apart by a fledgling Mekhet experimenting with Auspex aren't really conducive to that sort of game play.<br /> <br /> My personal preference also leans toward minimalism. I don't like maintaining a cache of 10 plus dice, five books, charts, cards, tokens, and Excel sheets just to PLAY a character and I don't like having to increase the totals of those things exponentially to RUN a game. Second edition has more rules. You only needed two books for first edition. You currently need four books (one of them technically being 1st edition) if you want to maintain a semblance of balance. Second edition is not very backwards compatible but first is forward compatible. Most of the stuff in 2nd was already in 1st as optional alternative mechanics. They just went from optional to mandatory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, there we go! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-22-2017, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T19:55:22-07:00","id":1082103,"title":"","content":"There's no real comparison or metaphor other than a reboot, because that's essentially what it was.<br /> <br /> Both Vampires share the same basic setting; the real world plus some supernatural gloss. The gloss is a different shade in each, but it's still the same world until you get to the details of supernatural societies.<br /> <br /> Vampires, throughout other media and history, have huge variation. Both Requiem and Masquerade, however, share blood points/pool, blood bonds, The Kiss and general feeding methods, torpor, bloodlines, Clans (down to names and themes for some), disciplines (down to names and themes and powers for some to most), (some, if not all) weaknesses, (some, if not all) strengths, (some, if not all) themes, (most, if not all) inspirations, blood sorcery (if different styles of it), and other things I've probably missed.<br /> <br /> Calling them different editions really isn't all that far-fetched. They're more similar than they're different, in the end. The only reason they would look very different would be because you're already a fan. From the grand perspective of all vampire fiction and how incredibly varied that can be, they're basically the same.<br /> <br /> The closest equivalent I can think of would be Traveller, which has editions published from like seven different publishers, two of which are concurrent. Admittedly, the differences between those settings are less than between the *oD lines.<br /> <br /> In the end, it doesn't matter whether you call them different editions or not, so long as you just let people play their preferred setting in peace.<br /> <br /> It might be better to open a new thread if people want to continue this, though. As stated by others, we're far off course here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T20:29:00-07:00","id":1082114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082083#post1082083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, who published it is less relevant to the distinction between the games than the fact that they are set in different fictional worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but D&amp;D doesnt really have a &quot;World&quot; it has setting elements.....and thats about it. I think you were more on point with the Amazing spiderman &amp; Spiderman 3 analogy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081934#post1081934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone liking one thing or another shouldn't have any bearing on this situation except to possibly take sides. But the idea of 'going backwards' seems to be a perception based on your past experience. I played Requiem first, never had to make a decision about which to play, because I wasn't interested in Masquerade. My experience could offer me a lot of arguments that, vary from yours or whoever elses, so its probably best to deal with the games as they are, rather than our own experiences with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I started with NWoD and i didnt read any of OWoD until Werewolf 20th was announced and yes it does feel like going backwards sometimes as there are some..... interesting design choices in the rules, on the vein of &quot;OH GOD WHO THOUGH THIS WAS A GOOD IDEA?&quot; that would just not fly in more modern games. Example look up the regeneration rules in Apocalypse, is a convoluted mess that it could just be bypassed so easily (Also, whoever said werewolves regenerated more in apocalypse is plain wrong) that is just morbidly fascinating reading that mechanic, like watching a caveman invent a oval shape rock to not use the wheel. Or things like Pure breed which was indicator that &quot;Balance&quot; was a foot note on the suggestion box back them.<br /> <br /> Or other choices that were so good that is kinda makes you shake your head that following version didnt carry them on. And for all the talk of NWoD/Chrod being a tool box, mage the ascension was the true tool box game of all the history of the WW/OPP games, never meet a game that told me:<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey dude, ever wanted to play amateur game designer?&quot;<br /> &quot;Not really but....&quot;<br /> &quot;Though luck kiddo!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T21:03:58-07:00","id":1082124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082114#post1082114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but D&amp;D doesnt really have a &amp;quot;World&amp;quot; it has setting elements.....and thats about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you never heard of the Forgotten Realms? Its lore is more in-depth and convoluted than the WoD metaplot by a significant margin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T23:08:47-07:00","id":1082161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082083#post1082083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but it is a very similar conversation to comparing Golarion's elves (from Pathfinder) with Faerun's elves (from D&amp;D). They share the same name, and the settings share a lot of tropes, but they do not have continuity between them, so it's weird to talk about &quot;nerfs&quot; or &quot;buffs&quot; between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, then I think we are just arguing over semantics.<br /> <br /> For these two statements:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>&quot;<i>Masquerade Celerity felt more powerful as it gave you extra actions per turn, while in Requiem, Celerity concentrates more on defense and movement, with active use being just an initiative jump.&quot;</i></li> <li>&quot;<i>Celerity is one of the disciplines that got nerfed in Requiem from Masquerade.</i>&quot;</li> </ol>The first one is fine, but the second one peeves your pets, as it were? As long as you're not actually invalidating comparisons between Spheres and Arcana or Requiem Blood Potency and Masquerade Generation, then I think we are good. Don't call one a sequel, call it a reboot or a spiritual successor. <br /> <br /> If we're not arguing semantics and you are arguing that there isn't any continuity between Requiem and Masquerade, and that there isn't any continuity between Pathfinder elves and Forgotten Realms elves - let me put it this way.<br /> <br /> There is no direct continuity between chimpanzees and humans. Humans did not evolve from, evolve into, or replace any of the chimps living today. No chimp is going to naturally birth a human kid. But humans and chimps do have a common ancestor and share a significant chunk of DNA. If you don't recognize those connections you are leaving out a major element of their relationship. Humans and chimps do have a connection that is closer and a relationship that is more statistically important than the connection between humans and crocodiles or humans and trees. Pathfinder and Forgotten Realm elves have similar common ancestors and DNA. Earlier D&amp;D editions for sure, Tolkein elves before that. 'The evolution of elves in fiction and gaming' is probably a paper out there somewhere.<br /> <br /> To come back around, you can trace the changes to the Fighter character class between editions / retellings / versions / successors / incarnations / reboots / franchises of D&amp;D, including everything from Chainmail to Spelljammer to Pathfinder. You can then argue the pros and cons for which one you think is the most powerful or best version. That's a legitimate conversation about mechanics in games with at least a common ancestor but also including sequels and new editions. I don't think it's fair to discount the mechanical, literary <i>and</i> creative continuities of these game lines just because there might not be timeline or direct-setting continuity. <br /> <br /> If one person says that the Gangrel Clan Flaw isn't as limiting in the Requiem edition as opposed to Masquerade - you can either argue the point (Actually, it's more limiting because X), or you can argue semantics (by saying we should really call it more of a successor than an edition). <br /> <br /> In the end, its coming across to me like you are saying that Requiem Ventrue are no more connected to Masquerade Ventrue than Pathfinder Elves are to Keebler Elves. That's what I'm having a hard time with. When someone says &quot;Chimps and humans are different species,&quot; followed by &quot;Tomatoes and humans are also different species.&quot; they have stated two true facts. But they have left out a very significant part of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T04:53:54-07:00","id":1082211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082099#post1082099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, there we go! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lot of thread to read through, but there's been some disagreement with tsusasi's post. I personally think 2E is an all around improvement, and that the single core book in 2E corresponds to both core books in 1E. The other books tsusasi refers to contains optional subsystems that weren't present in the 1E core books either.<br /> <br /> Edit: And the God-Machine rules update is still available for free if you want a more expansive list of Merits in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-22-2017, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T05:59:13-07:00","id":1082222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082211#post1082211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a lot of thread to read through, but there's been some disagreement with tsusasi's post. I personally think 2E is an all around improvement, and that the single core book in 2E corresponds to both core books in 1E. The other books tsusasi refers to contains optional subsystems that weren't present in the 1E core books either.<br /> <br /> Edit: And the God-Machine rules update is still available for free if you want a more expansive list of Merits in 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be honest, once I started hearing about changes that 2E made, I really didn't like the sound of them. Like the entire concept of touch stones as a form of game mechanic, instead of an organic role playing component. I get it, touch stones are supposed to keep you tied to the remains of your humanity. But really, why did that have to be written up with a rule system, instead of letting it flow naturally as part of the story? I don't need a dice roll to tell me if my character goes into a rage frenzy over seeing their biological child being murdered!<br /> <br /> <br /> The Strix were also an addition that I don't see much point in. The entire premise of vampire was that they are solitary, back stabbing predators by their very nature. Giving them an outside threat to rally around really detracts from that concept of personal horror and gradual descent into a cold, uncaring monster. Besides, I thought they already had enough enemies to compete with, without adding a unique villain tailored for them. The Strix also tried to impose some level of origin point or time period in which vampires emerged into the world, which ruins the ambiguity that 1E had in which it's left up to the player's imagination on where vampires came from.<br /> <br /> There's probably some other changes I didn't like the sound of, but I can't remember them. But the Strix and touch stones stand out the most in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-22-2017, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:14:42-07:00","id":1082223,"title":"","content":"Touchstones got rules because without rules you don't really have any incentive to have Touchstones. The rules also reinforce the themes of having to cling on to humanity or descending into becoming a monster. It's the same reason Humanity has a rule system. So that the themes of the game isn't separated from the actual rules of the game.<br /> But if you don't like them you could just not use them. They're just added on top of the basic Humanity system so it's not a problem to just excise.<br /> <br /> Strix are optional. And were added in a 1E supplement first.<br /> Also, I don't get why you think of vampires as solitary creatures when they're all about forming coteries, joining covenants and participating in their own societies filled with other vampires. Backstabbing is incredibly accurate, but solitary is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:18:47-07:00","id":1082226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082124#post1082124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you never heard of the Forgotten Realms? Its lore is more in-depth and convoluted than the WoD metaplot by a significant margin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but forgotten realms is <b><u>a</u></b> setting of D&amp;D (just like planescape, spelljammer, midnight, raveloft, Dark sun, etc) that until 5e was made the default one. You read the core manuals on 3rd and back and there was not much setting to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:24:45-07:00","id":1082228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1077584#post1077584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And yeah, for the templates, while it seems they tried to have some balance in 1e (werewolves were pretty nerfed</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I would hardly call <b>complete regeneration every round</b> to be 'nerfed' in a game that revolves around hunting in packs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082223#post1082223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touchstones got rules because without rules you don't really have any incentive to have Touchstones. The rules also reinforce the themes of having to cling on to humanity or descending into becoming a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not the case for experienced story tellers (not Story Teller, but actual story tellers). You can portray the struggle for humanity without attaching a rule system to it. Once you add dice pools to keeping up with your family (or whatever), instead of making it part of an organic experience, it becomes less compelling as a narrative and feels more like a chore you have to keep tabs on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-22-2017, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:36:29-07:00","id":1082231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082222#post1082222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't need a dice roll to tell me if my character goes into a rage frenzy over seeing their biological child being murdered!</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on that you probably shouldn't be playing any edition of vampire, since... you know, frenzy has always rules like that. That the system is codified rather than in players whims.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Giving them an outside threat to rally around really detracts from that concept of personal horror and gradual descent into a cold, uncaring monster. </div> </div> </div>Except vampires don't rally together against the strix. They become paranoid and start doing their backstabbing Now rather in the next twenty years. They have to start playing the cards they've been keeping for years, so that the important events happen during the game rather than twenty years after your players play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Strix also tried to impose some level of origin point or time period in which vampires emerged into the world, which ruins the ambiguity that 1E had in which it's left up to the player's imagination on where vampires came from. </div> </div> </div>No. That's a complete misconception on your part. Vampires do not have an origin point or time period in which they emerged into the world, especially not one because of the strix (especially since the books specifically say that everything they say conflicts with another and they specifically enjoy messing with kindred). The first chapter in the book has three conflicting origins for each clan for godsake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:37:55-07:00","id":1082233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082228#post1082228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would hardly call <b>complete regeneration every round</b> to be 'nerfed' in a game that revolves around hunting in packs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E werewolves only regenerated a single bashing each round, or one lethal per Essence spent. And they treated aggravated damage just like regular humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082228#post1082228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that's not the case for experienced story tellers (not Story Teller, but actual story tellers). You can portray the struggle for humanity without attaching a rule system to it. Once you add dice pools to keeping up with your family (or whatever), instead of making it part of an organic experience, it becomes less compelling as a narrative and feels more like a chore you have to keep tabs on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do mind that experienced story tellers might not be the majority of the Story Tellers out there. Also, the very same things could be said about the underlying Humanity system. You could remove that and let the struggle to retain/regain your humanity be carried out through roleplaying alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:48:55-07:00","id":1082236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082226#post1082226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes but forgotten realms is <b><u>a</u></b> setting of D&amp;D (just like planescape, spelljammer, midnight, raveloft, Dark sun, etc) that until 5e was made the default one. You read the core manuals on 3rd and back and there was not much setting to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>3.x default setting was Greyhawk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:50:25-07:00","id":1082237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082233#post1082233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1E werewolves only regenerated a single bashing each round, or one lethal per Essence spent. And they treated aggravated damage just like regular humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do mind that experienced story tellers might not be the majority of the Story Tellers out there. Also, the very same things could be said about the underlying Humanity system. You could remove that and let the struggle to retain/regain your humanity be carried out through roleplaying alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Understandable. I got my start in role playing through online forums in which we nearly always did things with a sandbox method in regards to story telling. Instead of dice, charts and attributes, we did a collaborative story in which each player took turns adding to the story through the actions of their characters. To be perfectly honest, I have very little experience with hard rule style role playing. I've never even played Chronicles of Darkness, I just bough the books for the inspiration material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082231#post1082231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No. That's a complete misconception on your part. Vampires do not have an origin point or time period in which they emerged into the world, especially not one because of the strix (especially since the books specifically say that everything they say conflicts with another and they specifically enjoy messing with kindred). The first chapter in the book has three conflicting origins for each clan for godsake.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I want to clarify that I mentioned the Strix </span></span></span><i>tried</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to impose some level. Not a flat out answer. The fact that there are rumors which suggest the first vampires gained their powers from the Strix means that there is a possible origin point for them when it comes to the Strix chronicle. Maybe it's the truth, or maybe the owls are full of shit. Who knows?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T06:59:40-07:00","id":1082241,"title":"","content":"\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082222#post1082222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, why did that have to be written up with a rule system, instead of letting it flow naturally as part of the story?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically because of this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1079660#post1079660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally is the issue of freedom vs vision. 2nd edition mechanics gear towards A style of play while 1st edition have a bunch of mechanics that clumsily carry the game with little to no synergy between them. The latter makes ignoring certain mechanics for an alternative style of play easier while 2nd edition\u00b4s mechanics interface with its themes which at the same time makes it difficult to play it when you wanna play vampire but dont quite buy into those themes.<br /> <br /> Example 2nd puts lots of mechanical emphasis in Vampires dealing with their human lives, some people like to play that. Others like to play characters completely immersed in their supernatural lives without it being a &quot;thing&quot; as dealing with human life, friends or family is boring to them or their foregone conclusion is not something they care about. 2nd edition lets you play that character but it makes it a &quot;thing&quot; with consequences while in 1st it didnt.<br /> <br /> So someone that would like to play a vampire, like the setting but dont necessarily buy into 2nd edition themes could choose 1st edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082222#post1082222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Strix were also an addition that I don't see much point in. The entire premise of vampire was that they are solitary, back stabbing predators by their very nature. Giving them an outside threat to rally around really detracts from that concept of personal horror and gradual descent into a cold, uncaring monster. Besides, I thought they already had enough enemies to compete with, without adding a unique villain tailored for them. The Strix also tried to impose some level of origin point or time period in which vampires emerged into the world, which ruins the ambiguity that 1E had in which it's left up to the player's imagination on where vampires came from.<br /> <br /> There's probably some other changes I didn't like the sound of, but I can't remember them. But the Strix and touch stones stand out the most in my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah i agree the strix were badly handled for what requiem is supposed to be. I get their narrative use but it would be better if it wasnt just the strix but a system to generate your own vampire-like creatures that appeared as competitor/predators of the vampires and that the strix were one of the example ones. Kinda like the Idigam.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:11:55-07:00","id":1082248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082161#post1082161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For these two statements:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>&quot;<i>Masquerade Celerity felt more powerful as it gave you extra actions per turn, while in Requiem, Celerity concentrates more on defense and movement, with active use being just an initiative jump.&quot;</i></li> <li>&quot;<i>Celerity is one of the disciplines that got nerfed in Requiem from Masquerade.</i>&quot;</li> </ol>The first one is fine, but the second one peeves your pets, as it were?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. Though I do think it would be better to talk about Masquerade Celerity in the present tense, since Masquerade is still an actively supported game, but that's a very minior quibble. I still have a habit of speaking of WoD in the past tense at times as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082161#post1082161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as you're not actually invalidating comparisons between Spheres and Arcana or Requiem Blood Potency and Masquerade Generation, then I think we are good. Don't call one a sequel, call it a reboot or a spiritual successor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly don't intend to invalidate any and all comparison between them. It just rubs me the wrong way when those comparisons are talked about in the terms we as gamers typically use to describe changes between editions of a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082161#post1082161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, its coming across to me like you are saying that Requiem Ventrue are no more connected to Masquerade Ventrue than Pathfinder Elves are to Keebler Elves. That's what I'm having a hard time with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you are having a hard time with something I am not saying. I acknowledge that there is a connection, and a string connection at that, between WoD and CofD, and even concede that I understand why people often treat them like Editions of the same game. It just bothers me when they do so because that way of framing it diminishes the value of having both as separate games existing in parallel rather than concurrent versions of the same game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082161#post1082161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone says &quot;Chimps and humans are different species,&quot; followed by &quot;Tomatoes and humans are also different species.&quot; they have stated two true facts. But they have left out a very significant part of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that analogy also leaves out a very significant portion of the conversation that's been going on. If someone was talking about the evolutionary changes between humans and chimpanzees, as if humans had evolved from chimpanzees, &quot;we have a common ancestor, but humans didn't evolve from chimpanzees any more than we evolved from tomatoes&quot; would be an appropriate response, in my opinion. The analogy might be a little extreme, but it isn't being made for no reason - the point is to compare to another, similar relationship where the difference between sharing a common ancestor and having evolutionary continuity is more obvious, in order to more clearly illustrate the point that humans do not share evolutionary continuity with chimpanzees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-22-2017, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T07:26:52-07:00","id":1082258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082237#post1082237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understandable. I got my start in role playing through online forums in which we nearly always did things with a sandbox method in regards to story telling. Instead of dice, charts and attributes, we did a collaborative story in which each player took turns adding to the story through the actions of their characters. To be perfectly honest, I have very little experience with hard rule style role playing. I've never even played Chronicles of Darkness, I just bough the books for the inspiration material. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason you can't still do that. You roleplayed freestyle without feeling constrained by the rules before, why would you suddenly feel constrained by the rules just because they changed?<br /> <br /> Not everyone can play this way. For some people, saying, &quot;it's important for vampires to maintain connections to humanity&quot; in the book doesn't mean anything unless there are mechanical benefits for doing so or drawbacks for not doing so. If you would prefer to leave that sort of thing purely to roleplay with no mechanics backing it up, more power to you! But the game is not worse for including those mechanics for people who want or need them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082237#post1082237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I want to clarify that I mentioned the Strix </span></span></span><i>tried</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> to impose some level. Not a flat out answer. The fact that there are rumors which suggest the first vampires gained their powers from the Strix means that there is a possible origin point for them when it comes to the Strix chronicle. Maybe it's the truth, or maybe the owls are full of shit. Who knows?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>[/quote]<br /> There have always been rumors about possible origins for vampires, since the 1e core book. Granted, the 1e core book was lighter on them, and heavier on the &quot;nobody knows!!!&quot;, but by simple nature of expanding content, more and more rumors gradually get added. By the 1e Clan books, it was suggested that vampires don't have a single origin, and that some of the rumors are probably true for specific groups of vampires but that definitely none of them are true for all vampires. This was also the first time the Strix started being mentioned. 2e did nothing new in this regard, it just expanded on things that have been part of the game for nearly a decade. If you don't want any of the rumors to be true in your games, they are not. Simple as that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T08:23:39-07:00","id":1082272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082248#post1082248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. Though I do think it would be better to talk about Masquerade Celerity in the present tense, since Masquerade is still an actively supported game, but that's a very minior quibble. I still have a habit of speaking of WoD in the past tense at times as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Masquerade is supported <i>again</i>, not <i>still</i>. For seven years it was an unsupported franchise that had reached a logical conclusion (Gehenna) and had been completely rebooted as Requiem. V20 brought Masquerade back from the dead and Paradox now intends to give it and the old World of Darkness a full, new life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082248#post1082248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly don't intend to invalidate any and all comparison between them. It just rubs me the wrong way when those comparisons are talked about in the terms we as gamers typically use to describe changes between editions of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm going to forgive the person who says the edition of Vampire after <i>Masquerade: Revised</i> was <i>Requiem: 1st Edition</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082248#post1082248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you are having a hard time with something I am not saying. I acknowledge that there is a connection, and a string connection at that, between WoD and CofD, and even concede that I understand why people often treat them like Editions of the same game. It just bothers me when they do so because that way of framing it diminishes the value of having both as separate games existing in parallel rather than concurrent versions of the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying<i> Requiem and Masquerade are two different editions of Vampire</i> is a more accurate statement than saying <i>Requiem and Masquerade are two entirely separate game-lines that have no continuity.</i> So trying to correct the first statement by offering the second only muddies the conversation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082248#post1082248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that analogy also leaves out a very significant portion of the conversation that's been going on. If someone was talking about the evolutionary changes between humans and chimpanzees, as if humans had evolved from chimpanzees, &quot;we have a common ancestor, but humans didn't evolve from chimpanzees any more than we evolved from tomatoes&quot; would be an appropriate response, in my opinion. The analogy might be a little extreme, but it isn't being made for no reason - the point is to compare to another, similar relationship where the difference between sharing a common ancestor and having evolutionary continuity is more obvious, in order to more clearly illustrate the point that humans do not share evolutionary continuity with chimpanzees.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think your analogy here is extreme, I actually agree with it because you recognize the common ancestor right in the statement. You can talk about the evolutionary changes between chimps and humans as long as you are using the reference point of the common ancestor. Saying that when they evolved within the genus, humans got a buff to intelligence and stamina while chimps got a buff to physical strength and aggression may be a weird way to say it, but it gets the point across. And once a person can recognize and accept that common ancestors and genera are both forms of continuity (even though not direct continuity), I think most will see that there's an even greater argument to be made that Requiem did evolve directly from Masquerade, unlike chimps and humans who do only share that common ancestor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T12:03:49-07:00","id":1082340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082272#post1082272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Masquerade is supported <i>again</i>, not <i>still</i>. For seven years it was an unsupported franchise that had reached a logical conclusion (Gehenna) and had been completely rebooted as Requiem. V20 brought Masquerade back from the dead and Paradox now intends to give it and the old World of Darkness a full, new life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. It's a minor clarification to a minor quibble aI had, but yes, this is accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082272#post1082272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm going to forgive the person who says the edition of Vampire after <i>Masquerade: Revised</i> was <i>Requiem: 1st Edition</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your prerogative. Personally, it irks me when people do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082272#post1082272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying<i> Requiem and Masquerade are two different editions of Vampire</i> is a more accurate statement than saying <i>Requiem and Masquerade are two entirely separate game-lines that have no continuity.</i> So trying to correct the first statement by offering the second only muddies the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. To use your own evolution analogy, saying humans and chimpanzees are too completely separate species with no evolutionary continuity is more accurate than saying humans are an evolution of chimpanzees. The former is true, if arguably under-representative of their commonality. The latter is not true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082272#post1082272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think your analogy here is extreme, I actually agree with it because you recognize the common ancestor right in the statement. You can talk about the evolutionary changes between chimps and humans as long as you are using the reference point of the common ancestor.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're using the common ancestor as the reference point, you're not comparing changes between chimps and humans, you're comparing the changes between <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chimpanzee\u2013human_last_common_ancestor\" target=\"_blank\">CHILA</a> and humans with the changes between CHILA and chimps. Likewise if you're comparing Masquerade Gangrel with Requiem Gangrel, you are comparing one game's take on the concept of feral vampires with another game's take on the same concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082272#post1082272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that when they evolved within the genus, humans got a buff to intelligence and stamina while chimps got a buff to physical strength and aggression may be a weird way to say it, but it gets the point across.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you would not say that humans got a nerf to strength and agression from chimpanzees because chimpanzees did not become humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082272#post1082272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And once a person can recognize and accept that common ancestors and genera are both forms of continuity (even though not direct continuity), I think most will see that there's an even greater argument to be made that Requiem did evolve directly from Masquerade, unlike chimps and humans who do only share that common ancestor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking about a different kind of continuity here. I'm not saying Requiem didn't evolve from Masquerade, I've quite consistently called it a spiritual successor and conceded that despite my personal distaste of the comparisons I understand why they are commonly made. When I say there is no continuity between Masquerade and Requiem I am talking about narrative continuity. Masquerade's narrative continuity ended with Gehenna, though it is soon to be advanced again much like when Doctor Who came back after having been ended for several years. Requiem's narrative continuity started from a nebulous toolbox and gradually extended backwards to flesh out the setting's history, and at no point do the two meet (at least not by default assumptions. A Storyteller could of course create narrative continuity between them because toolbox, but people could they create narrative continuity between The Flinstones and Star Trek if they wanted.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T12:56:09-07:00","id":1082360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082241#post1082241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Basically because of this<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehhh, if that's the way the players want to run their characters then I think the problem isn't about mechanical consequences, but rather their personal play style. If you're not interested in organically role playing the descent into an undead monster, then chances are adding mechanical systems isn't going to help. You don't suddenly become invested in role playing the tragic loss of a loved one just because you botch a die roll. That comes naturally to you as a role player by seeing the world from the character's perspective. If you can't portray your character's emotions without the game telling you &quot;you feel bad about yourself now&quot; then it might be better to play a vampire who already has a low humanity threshold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T13:14:19-07:00","id":1082369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying Requiem and Masquerade are two different editions of Vampire is a more accurate statement than saying Requiem and Masquerade are two entirely separate game-lines that have no continuity. So trying to correct the first statement by offering the second only muddies the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082340#post1082340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's not. To use your own evolution analogy, saying humans and chimpanzees are too completely separate species with no evolutionary continuity is more accurate than saying humans are an evolution of chimpanzees. The former is true, if arguably under-representative of their commonality. The latter is not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is. You've changed the statements in your comparison and I agree in that case. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082340#post1082340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're using the common ancestor as the reference point, you're not comparing changes between chimps and humans, you're comparing the changes between CHILA and humans with the changes between CHILA and chimps. Likewise if you're comparing Masquerade Gangrel with Requiem Gangrel, you are comparing one game's take on the concept of feral vampires with another game's take on the same concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree on the first sentence. Disagree on the second, because once again you are leaving out the big part of the story that Requiem directly evolved from Masquerade and that Gangrel from one were billed and seen as a replacement / reskin to the other. It's not comparing feral vampires in Masquerade to feral vampires in the Witcher games or Ravenloft. Comparing the intelligence of humans and tomatoes is not usefully analogous to comparing the intelligence between chimps and humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082340#post1082340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but you would not say that humans got a nerf to strength and agression from chimpanzees because chimpanzees did not become humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. While you <i>would</i> have a far better case in saying Requiem Ventrue got a nerf to their disciplines and a buff to their Clan bane from Masquerade Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082340#post1082340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking about a different kind of continuity here. I'm not saying Requiem didn't evolve from Masquerade, I've quite consistently called it a spiritual successor and conceded that despite my personal distaste of the comparisons I understand why they are commonly made. When I say there is no continuity between Masquerade and Requiem I am talking about narrative continuity. Masquerade's narrative continuity ended with Gehenna, though it is soon to be advanced again much like when Doctor Who came back after having been ended for several years. Requiem's narrative continuity started from a nebulous toolbox and gradually extended backwards to flesh out the setting's history, and at no point do the two meet (at least not by default assumptions. A Storyteller could of course create narrative continuity between them because toolbox, but people could they create narrative continuity between The Flinstones and Star Trek if they wanted.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Narrative continuity is not the only type of continuity that should count when relating things to each other. The creative team, the game line, the publisher, the mechanics (See Maina's list) - those all have their own continuities themselves. And lets look at the Lexicon - where do you put that? Maybe you quibble and say its a literary continuity and not a narrative continuity, further narrowing the definition of narrative continuity to only the IC timeline. Just because there isn't a made up historical event or NPC that exists in both gamelines simultaneously doesn't mean (I would argue) you get to discount all the other continuities.<br /> <br /> Any decent ST can connect any two franchises, that's true. But you're gonna have a far easier time doing that for Masquerade to Requiem than for Masquerade to Star Trek. And remember, this is exactly what many tabletop and LARP groups did in 2004 - they transferred their games (which included their narrative continuity) from Masquerade to Requiem. Not every campaign ended or rebooted entirely. You still see Masquerade disciplines and mechanics being converted for Requiem on these boards, while I don't ever remember any threads converting Masquerade mechanics to a Flintstones RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T13:52:07-07:00","id":1082381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1081917#post1081917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S. Brechen's argument is that these games are direct continuations and that them being 'different games' is a falsehood, and some sort of spin on behalf of the publisher that attempts to cover that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. No.<br /> <br /> No. I accept that you can call them different games, but I disagree, or at any rate, I personally refuse to consider them unrelated games. As far as being a &quot;direct continuation&quot; of each other, I would rather say NWoD was built on the remains of the OWoD. All I will agree with is that this is a complicated case and that I don't see why it should be officially wrong to say that CoD is the continuation of the oWoD as it was when it ended.<br /> <br /> Let me offer an alternative to my statement :<br /> <br /> I consider (in particular) Vampire the Requiem 1e to be reboot of (and directly insp\u00eered by) Vampire Revised. I am counting out 20th anniversary edition and whatever name the upcoming editions will bear, because, yes, that would be incorrect to say that Requiem 2e comes from Masquerade 20th and that changes were made between those two games since the branching already happened.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now as for the chimpanzee argument that is filled with intentional misintepreting to keep things going, here :<br /> <br /> Masquerade Revised = Lucy (let's say Lucy IS the common ancestor even though she actually isn't)<br /> <br /> Humans = Requiem 1e<br /> <br /> Requiem 20th Anniversary = Chimps (yeah, for this contrived comparison, I equate Requiem with chimps, sue me)<br /> <br /> D&amp;D 3574000th edition = Star Fruit<br /> <br /> So no, Humans don't have changes compared to chimps, but they do have changes compared to Lucy. Of course, that doesn't mean you can draw parallels between chimps and humans, but that hasn't been my point here. I've been talking about the relationship between the NWoD and the OWoD as it was when it ended with Time of Judgement.<br /> <br /> <br /> So what, was Requiem 1e &quot;Awlays meant&quot; to be a gloriously independent game from Masquerade Revised ? Seriously, in all the writers involved in ALL the books from that (Re 1e) line, would all agree to those exact terms ? Even if they did, would all players wo made the transition agree to those terms ? So they don't have inside information, big deal, they're players, death of the author takes a whole new dimention in RPGs.<br /> <br /> Sure, Masquerade and Requiem are different in lots of ways. Anyone can also see that the authors of Requiem 1e read Masquerade revised extensively, liked the Ventrue, bossy assholes, and Nosferatu ugly sewer mafia, and shifted one thing or two and came up with the totally original clans of Ventrue, bossy assholes, and Nosferaty, creepy sewer mafia, for Requiem 1e. They saw a bunch of disciplines and copy pasted most of their names and general areas of powers, sometimes to the precise type of power. Sure, they took Presence and renamed it Majesty, but it's kinda the same. Then, there was the Malkovian debacle, etc. That doesn't strike me as things people who wanted to create a completely original work would do. Maybe they were told to do it because otherwise it wouldn't sell to gamers who wouldn't recognize anything and be confused, but I don't know about the totally original game that didn't get made, I know about Requiem 1e.<br /> <br /> Now sure, there are differences, some big, some small. The mood and themes ? Yeah, I guess. Requiem wanted to avoid big fuck off elders controlling the world from the shadows and have a more local and more street level setting to focus on personal horror (ha ha). Of course, just because the game states that theme obviously means all players only did campaigns of &quot;personal horror&quot; and those who didn't just played the game wrong or something.<br /> <br /> So my point, really, is that there's no ONE correct way to see this issue. Charlaquin, you said you didn't like people talking about Requiem and Masquerade as &quot;editions&quot; (that's your prerogative, although I don't have to share it), but then, you also gave the example of the different versions of D&amp;D and that nobody compared D&amp;D 3rd edition and D&amp;D 4rth edition because they're recognozed as different games, which is fair, except they are indeed called, in this case, &quot;editions&quot;, so to go back to one of my previous question : What, exactly constitutes an edition, if not an arbitrary word used by a given publisher to sort out a bunch of books for a commercial purpose, so that when a gamer comes to the store and asks for D&amp;D 3rd edition, they get what thet asked for ?<br /> <br /> And so, what is a &quot;game&quot; ? Well, I don't know. I'd say a game is, the same way, a way to refer to a certain set of rules as they are presented in a certain book or series of books. So, if you as me, Requiem 1e and Requiem 2e are two different games. There are differences between the two, they're not HUGE (although they are big enough that you can't take a lot of 1e things for granted), but they are there. Similarly, Requiem 1e and Masquerade Revised are different games. The differences are pretty big, although there are a good deal of similarities. Also, Masquerade Revised and Shadowrun 5e are different games. They have almost nothing in common, but they are both games and they're different, so they're distinct games I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is my point, you can take those words and make them mean anything you want, because there is no deep inalterable truth here. I've never been made aware of commandments on the stone tablets that go &quot;Thou shalt only refer to editions if the games share the same themes and have a few rule changes, and don't ask me to explain how much is a few, thou shalt also know that and stop bothering me.&quot;, so really, we are just arguing about what terms we feel are appropriate and what comparisons we feel are worth making, and well, yes and compared Werewolf Revised to Forsaken 1e, because I feel those two games are close enough that I could make that comparison. Don't like that ? Well, I didn't do it to make anyone feel bad, I'd like to apologize if I did. Still don't feel it's a problem, though, but I should have shut up after that because that became an argument of epic proportions compared to what is a goddamn vocabulary preference non-issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","user":"S. Brechen","date":". 04-22-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T15:23:14-07:00","id":1082406,"title":"","content":"Look, we're arguing in ridiculous circles here. At the end of the day, I am not looking to disregard the connection between WoD and CofD. Yes, CofD is a spiritual successor to WoD. Yes, it was originally billed as a reboot. No, they are not different Editions of the same game - they have different settings, different fictional histories, different mechanics, different themes, different moods, different goals, different target audiences, albeit with a lot of crossover in some of those areas. No, I don't think it's wrong to compare and contrast the two. Yes, it still annoys me when people compare them <i>as they would compare mechanics from two editions of the same franchise</i>. You don't have to agree with me about that. I get why people do it and have said as much repeatedly. I can't help but feel like this whole conversation boils down to<br /> <br /> Me: I don't like it when people do [thing]<br /> People: But we do [thing] because [reasons]<br /> Me: I know. I still don't like it because [other reasons.]<br /> People: But we do it because [reasons]!<br /> Me: O... k... that's fine, I just don't care for it because [other reasons].<br /> People: But [reasons]!!!<br /> <br /> Like... can't I just not like when people do that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T16:12:52-07:00","id":1082423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082360#post1082360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't suddenly become invested in role playing the tragic loss of a loved one just because you botch a die roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about the frenzy roll then you misunderstand. It's not about what the character feels. It's about the unpredictable reaction arising from that situation. That's the game part of role-playing games. There's absolutely nothing wrong with free form role-playing, but it's not for everyone. When I play VtR or any other role-playing game I do it because I want an experience that is, in its core, a game, in contrast to free form role-playing that, to me, is something more akin to improv storytelling. I'm still in total control of my character's actions (except for special circumstances, such as in Frenzy, but that's why he's mastered Coil of the Wyrm) but not the consequences. It's both the thrill of the uncertainty, and a storytelling device that has led to many situations, both comical and dramatic, that would've never come up if we would've put away the dice.<br /> <br /> Your way of playing is not the wrong way of playing, but you seem to have misconceptions about why other people play it differently. And it kinda irked me because it reminded me of how elitistic some other free-form roleplayers have been in regard to playing styles on another forum I've frequented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-23-2017, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T19:30:32-07:00","id":1082490,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">\u200bLet's get back on to the topic of &quot;reasons to run 1st edition Vampire&quot; instead of arguing whether Requiem constitutes a new edition of Masquerade or not. The topic is not about Masquerade at all, the OP was asking about different editions of Requiem. If you want to engage in the discussion of whether you feel Requiem qualifies as a new edition of Masquerade you can start a new topic in the general cWoD forum.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T06:50:23-07:00","id":1082995,"title":"","content":"Generally, I prefer 1e because of its familiarity and I always run a Modified 1e Setting (just Rule Zero out the emotional deadness fluff that went nowhere and there you go). I don't like the reworked disciplines or things such as Conditions and Touchstones, and the new fluff such as the increased prominence of the Strix are also off-putting.<br /> <br /> I generally dislike the changes 2e CofD made in general when compared to 1e nWoD. So, I am totally on board with people running 1e instead of 2e, because some of us, such as myself, just prefer 1e over 2e and feel more comfortable with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T09:21:22-07:00","id":1083046,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't think it's even Rule Zero-ing out certain 1e corebook aspects, when even later books in the same edition pretend they never existed. The emotional deadness fluff was very quickly given the old silent treatment. Most other aspects are pretty easy to remove, like you can remove the Predator's Taint without largely affecting any other sub-systems, and now suddenly you can actually have a semi-functioning Society of the Night without having everyone risk freaking out every time they meet someone new. Other things are a little tricky, like removing the link between capital-M objective Morality and mental illness, which I've talked about so much in different areas, because the Derangement system is so integral to multiple parts of 1e V:tR. The difficulty of excising that last bit without a major re-write of the system is one of the reasons I prefer 2e, because it does that work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:08:27-07:00","id":1083065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1083046#post1083046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't think it's even Rule Zero-ing out certain 1e corebook aspects, when even later books in the same edition pretend they never existed. The emotional deadness fluff was very quickly given the old silent treatment. Most other aspects are pretty easy to remove, like you can remove the Predator's Taint without largely affecting any other sub-systems, and now suddenly you can actually have a semi-functioning Society of the Night without having everyone risk freaking out every time they meet someone new. Other things are a little tricky, like removing the link between capital-M objective Morality and mental illness, which I've talked about so much in different areas, because the Derangement system is so integral to multiple parts of 1e V:tR. The difficulty of excising that last bit without a major re-write of the system is one of the reasons I prefer 2e, because it does that work for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I normally just chop out Humanity completely, along with Predator's Taint and the emotional deadness. I have made homebrew conversions of Requiem 1e to Big Eyes Small Mouth 1e and there you don't have to worry about Derangement systems or that pesky Humanity meter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T10:44:49-07:00","id":1083088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1083046#post1083046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most other aspects are pretty easy to remove, like you can remove the Predator's Taint without largely affecting any other sub-systems, and now suddenly you can actually have a semi-functioning Society of the Night without having everyone risk freaking out every time they meet someone new.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, even the 1E core book tells players that the Predator's Taint is often tossed out in homebrew because players feel that it's too much of a hassle. Which begs the question of why they would even write it up in the first place if they warn you how much of a problem it's going to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the emotionally dead stuff, I thought that was attributed to the Daeva who specifically use emotions like a tool to get what they want and eventually lose the ability to actually feel anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-24-2017, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T16:16:17-07:00","id":1083214,"title":"","content":"Rice vampire books were a heavy influence on R1. I think the emotionally dead stuff is about the &quot;Claudia effect&quot;. Vampires were unable to feel any new emotions. When someone would normally get angry, a vampire wouldn't feel angry. Instead the vampire would remember how it felt to be angry. It meant child vampires could grow intellectually but would remain emotionally stunted. No mechanics, just a roleplaying suggestion. I believe it might have evolved more into existing as a vampire can mess a person up so that even if one can do well at pretending to be human one still moves away from thinking like humans. The emotionally dead thing was an oddity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T17:52:30-07:00","id":1083242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1083214#post1083214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rice vampire books were a heavy influence on R1. I think the emotionally dead stuff is about the &amp;quot;Claudia effect&amp;quot;. Vampires were unable to feel any new emotions. When someone would normally get angry, a vampire wouldn't feel angry. Instead the vampire would remember how it felt to be angry. It meant child vampires could grow intellectually but would remain emotionally stunted. No mechanics, just a roleplaying suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a terrible idea in theory, but in practice it's very difficult for people who experience emotions to portray characters without emotion. And even harder to make such characters interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T20:40:27-07:00","id":1084840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1083242#post1083242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a terrible idea in theory, but in practice it's very difficult for people who experience emotions to portray characters without emotion. And even harder to make such characters interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree, but for a game that is supposed to allow for playing vampires from all sorts of media, where it so happens there are many examples of extremely emotional vampires, the idea of characters defaulting to any kind of deadened emotions didn't fit. It falls into the category of things people will often pretend doesn't exist, so there is no need to support it. I think it was part difficulty and part doesn't fit well known icons that killed the idea in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T19:21:14-07:00","id":1085284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1084840#post1084840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I tend to agree, but for a game that is supposed to allow for playing vampires from all sorts of media, where it so happens there are many examples of extremely emotional vampires, the idea of characters defaulting to any kind of deadened emotions didn't fit. It falls into the category of things people will often pretend doesn't exist, so there is no need to support it. I think it was part difficulty and part doesn't fit well known icons that killed the idea in practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I'm a bit of an apologist for...some...of the things people don't like about first edition Requiem, and I <i>never </i>liked the emotional deadness thing. Like, from a purely narrative standpoint, it's great. Tragic and horrifying...if you're writing a vampire novel. From the standpoint of &quot;this is improvisational pseudo-theatre that people have to act out&quot;, it doesn't work nearly as well for creating and playing an active character, especially given that so much of the game's aesthetic draws from Gothic media, which is, ya know, a branch of Romanticism. It's hard to bemoan your fallen state when it's more like, meh, kind of a drag, eh?<br /> <br /> That's not any kind of dig on the first edition writers; I totally see what they were going for, but that's what second editions are for...<br /> <br /> Fun fact: the first real Requiem game I played, my character became <i>more </i>emotionally aware when he became a vampire.<br /> <br /> As for the topic at hand (and here's my apologism coming through): I think first edition Requiem is great. If you want a game about vampires and politics and passion, and a fairly hands-off rules set, you could do much worse. I pretty much had the rules for vampires memorized before 2E came out, and I'm notoriously terrible at remembering rules at the gaming table.<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm on board the second edition train, but I'd absolutely play a first edition Requiem game if someone invited me to (partially because Vampire is my favourite and I never get to play it). Conversely, I probably wouldn't want to play a first edition Werewolf game, even though Forsaken Second Edition is among my top five for CofD games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T05:54:30-07:00","id":1086574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1082223#post1082223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't get why you think of vampires as solitary creatures when they're all about forming coteries, joining covenants and participating in their own societies filled with other vampires. Backstabbing is incredibly accurate, but solitary is not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Namely the fact that vampires do all that stuff because it is convenient for them to do so. Not because they feel any societal need for it. When the Beast rears its head and takes control, it's every man for themselves; fuck cooperation and social pleasantries. The core nature of a vampire is focused around their own survival. Everybody else are just tools to help them achieve that, or rivals which threaten their livelihood.<br /> <br /> Plus, do you really think the younger, newer vampires just flipped the switch and reverted to a medieval society of their own free will? No, they do so because the ones in charge can snuff them out at a moment's notice. If there's one thing that ensures a long, healthy relationship between leaders and serfs, it sure as hell isn't intimidation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2017, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T06:23:24-07:00","id":1086581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086574#post1086574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Namely the fact that vampires do all that stuff because it is convenient for them to do so. Not because they feel any societal need for it. When the Beast rears its head and takes control, it's every man for themselves; fuck cooperation and social pleasantries. The core nature of a vampire is focused around their own survival. Everybody else are just tools to help them achieve that, or rivals which threaten their livelihood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that's the reason animals started social groups in the first place; cooperation to ensure a higher rate of survival.<br /> That's not to say we humans don't care about each other unless it's for our personal benefit. We also have a psychological need to form societies. And considering that Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone are two of the five major covenants I'd say vampires, to a certain degree, also feel the need to belong.<br /> <br /> Besides, solitary describes behaviour rather than intent. It's certainly not a healthy society, but it's still there and it's upheld by vampires feeling a need (regardless of why that need is) to cooperate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:28:03-07:00","id":1086622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086581#post1086581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that's the reason animals started social groups in the first place; cooperation to ensure a higher rate of survival.<br /> That's not to say we humans don't care about each other unless it's for our personal benefit. We also have a psychological need to form societies. And considering that Lancea et Sanctum and Circle of the Crone are two of the five major covenants I'd say vampires, to a certain degree, also feel the need to belong.<br /> <br /> Besides, solitary describes behaviour rather than intent. It's certainly not a healthy society, but it's still there and it's upheld by vampires feeling a need (regardless of why that need is) to cooperate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, using human mentality doesn't really work for vampires, and using religious groups is the worst possible example. The Lancea Sanctum isn't so much a social group as it is a religious cult. I believe both editions make it clear that these are not your modern day, play nice Christians, either. They're the medieval, put-you-on-a-breaking-wheel-if-you-don't-convert style Christians. As for the Circle of the Crone, they're scattered and disorganized unless they're faced with a significant threat that encourages them to pool their resources together. First edition even states that mass genocide against pagan faiths is what lead to the founding of the covenant to begin with, they needed something to fight back against the Lancea; but that doesn't mean they necessarily wanted it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Invictus flat out reaffirms my claim as to them being a bunch of vicious sharks who will eat their wounded first chance they get. The Carthians are primarily formed out of young vampires who haven't fully realized the gravity of their situation and the Ordo are off doing whatever it is they do in the name of science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T10:30:15-07:00","id":1086696,"title":"","content":"I kinda see vampires as akin to lions in this matter. Cats are generally solitary by nature, but lions form prides because it is a more efficient way to hunt and to breed. However, they're still not great at living in social groups. There is a lot more infighting than you see with more social animals like wolves.<br /> <br /> Most &quot;solitary&quot; animals will form social groups out of necessity when food or other necessary resources are scarce, and sometimes this behavior is successful enough that it persists over multiple generations, making more social individuals more likely to pass on their genes. This may be why lions are some of the only pack-forming cats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:43:02-07:00","id":1086768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086696#post1086696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kinda see vampires as akin to lions in this matter. Cats are generally solitary by nature, but lions form prides because it is a more efficient way to hunt and to breed. However, they're still not great at living in social groups. There is a lot more infighting than you see with more social animals like wolves.<br /> <br /> Most &quot;solitary&quot; animals will form social groups out of necessity when food or other necessary resources are scarce, and sometimes this behavior is successful enough that it persists over multiple generations, making more social individuals more likely to pass on their genes. This may be why lions are some of the only pack-forming cats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is what I meant when I say they form groups because of convenience, not necessity. Its true that Lions form up into prides, but the male to female ratio is shockingly unbalanced. The male in charge wants all the girls to himself and sits around on his ass while the ladies bring him dinner. When another male starts to hit on his harem, they get into a fight over who gets to breeding rights with the loser either being kicked out or killed. A single male lion can mate 50 times a day, meaning that one male can have a harem of up to 50 lionesses all to himself without having to worry about an unsustainable population.<br /> <br /> <br /> Much the same way a single vampire could easily sustain themselves with a herd of 50 people without worrying about killing off their food supply from repeated feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T13:57:03-07:00","id":1086776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086768#post1086768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is what I meant when I say they form groups because of convenience, not necessity. Its true that Lions form up into prides, but the male to female ratio is shockingly unbalanced. The male in charge wants all the girls to himself and sits around on his ass while the ladies bring him dinner. When another male starts to hit on his harem, they get into a fight over who gets to breeding rights with the loser either being kicked out or killed. A single male lion can mate 50 times a day, meaning that one male can have a harem of up to 50 lionesses all to himself without having to worry about an unsustainable population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that surprising, lots of animals exhibit similar behavior. Also, while the male to female ratio is always very steep, but it's not always only one male. Usually only one <i>breeding</i> male, but other males aren't always driven off or killed. 1-3 males in a pride is pretty common. At any rate, it probably started out due to necessity, but over a few generations the ones that are willing to work together are the ones reproducing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086768#post1086768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much the same way a single vampire could easily sustain themselves with a herd of 50 people without worrying about killing off their food supply from repeated feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, yes, but in modern times this is extremely difficult in practice. The Masquerade becomes a concern with modern information technology, and with extremely large populations clustered in relatively small areas, vampires are going to run into a lot of competition. Not for vessels, but for territory. So, much like lions, vampires likely began forming social groups out of necessity despite being better suited for solitude by nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T15:25:18-07:00","id":1086830,"title":"","content":"I prefer to view vampire society like prison society. Everybody has their own self-interests. You can find like minded fellows or watch your back and don't drop the soap. You'll likely get screwed no matter what you do at some point, but you're not in Disneyland. What do you expect?<br /> <br /> At their worst vampires can be junkies that can literally rip your arms off if you make them angry. The only options in avoiding them are death, torpor, or becoming a near mindless junkie that rips people's arms off when you get angry. Given those alternatives, you might as well learn to live with your kindred. Strength in numbers and misery loves company.<br /> <br /> Tigers tend to be extremely territorial and solitary hunters, but lock a group in a cage and feed them well, they will usually not kill anybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T16:14:05-07:00","id":1086853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086830#post1086830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tigers tend to be extremely territorial and solitary hunters, but lock a group in a cage and feed them well, they will usually not kill anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're a dumbass who tries to hop inside and play with them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T20:57:29-07:00","id":1086989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086830#post1086830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer to view vampire society like prison society. Everybody has their own self-interests. You can find like minded fellows or watch your back and don't drop the soap. You'll likely get screwed no matter what you do at some point, but you're not in Disneyland. What do you expect?<br /> <br /> At their worst vampires can be junkies that can literally rip your arms off if you make them angry. The only options in avoiding them are death, torpor, or becoming a near mindless junkie that rips people's arms off when you get angry. Given those alternatives, you might as well learn to live with your kindred. Strength in numbers and misery loves company.<br /> <br /> Tigers tend to be extremely territorial and solitary hunters, but lock a group in a cage and feed them well, they will usually not kill anybody.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, prisoners and predators in captivity are being kept there by someone. Vampires work together by choice. There's no wardens or zookeepers forcing vampires to join Covenants. They do it for their own survival in the face of limited resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:44:06-07:00","id":1087292,"title":"","content":"I would throw in that Danse Macabre gave us 3 levels of covenant play. And at tier 1 covenants are exactly this ramshackle organizations in with most vampires roam free and just band together in face of a bigger threat. Something like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FyYMAFTmK8A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FyYMAFTmK8A\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FyYMAFTmK8A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FyYMAFTmK8A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Minus the silly coats I guess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12924-orzhov","name":"Orzhov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T15:43:00-07:00","id":1087365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1086989#post1086989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, prisoners and predators in captivity are being kept there by someone. Vampires work together by choice. There's no wardens or zookeepers forcing vampires to join Covenants. They do it for their own survival in the face of limited resources.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And it's a depicted as being a dark interpretation of political systems in which everybody is looking after themselves, first and foremost, complete with smear campaigns and assassinations of political rivals. When faced with an outside threat, they put on a display of unity. When left to their own devices, they turn to infighting, whether they do so openly or through covert actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am not saying vampires are incapable of working together, I am saying that their reasons for working together are completely different from those of a human's. Or at the very least they gradually become that way over the passage of time. Young vampires may be able to keep in touch with their humanity, but it is very rare to find an elder (who's seen some shit) who feels the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T03:31:24-07:00","id":1087602,"title":"","content":"I remembered started a thread a while back where asked a question about Requiem where I forgot to specify that I wanted info on 1E. I let slip that I was wary of 2E because of the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I said that my problem was that it effectively made the rest of the WoD a sci-fi (or whatever people wish to call it) where in every setting we now had to accept that just behind the curtain there was a bunch of nuts and bolts that were controlling everything. It was kind of like when you watch a movie with a twist you think is lame, you really enjoyed the rest of the movie,but now you have to judge the whole flick based on the twist, which ruins the whole movie. I was also looking forward to Demon: the Descent, which I hoped would effectively expand on the Inferno demons,and correct the problems with the Fallen, instead we got something which I found... really weird. It would have been fine as something of an AI splat (&quot;Robot: The Activated&quot;? &quot;Android: The Programmed&quot;?) but as demons it was just too weird, even for WoD at its most creative. In both oWoD and CoD the splats are still fundamentally the same as their mythological/folklore inspirations, vampires are still vampires, werewolves are still werewolves and so on, but the same cannot be said of demons in DTF.<br /> <br /> I've learned to separate what I like and what I don't like, and DTF and the God machine are not in my personal &quot;canon&quot;, which has allowed me to enjoy CoD the way I used to, even 2E content. My hope is that they don't make the God Machine so omnipresent throughout the CoD that it becomes too difficult to ignore it.<br /> <br /> That said there are still reasons to play 1E: you may want to make use of a lot of the wealth of content built up throughout 1E and most of the stuff exclusive to 2E can be ignored or replaced, easier than adapting a whole bunch of 1E stuff to 2E. Basically, depending on how much content from 1E you want to make use of it might just be easier to go full 1E. Then there's also the question of source-books like Inferno, one of my personal favorites, which from what I understand is 100% incompatible with 2E rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T03:48:47-07:00","id":1087608,"title":"","content":"The good thing about the God-Machine is that it's completely optional, just like all the other gamelines. Only MtA would lose out since it's all about Mysteries and the other gamelines are good sources for them.<br /> <br /> About compatibility; Vampire is the gameline that is the most compatible to the previous edition. Much of the stuff doesn't need any adaptation at all, and the few things that do need it just need a little touch up (such as a new XP cost for Gifts of the Alu, or new target numbers for rituals). The only exception that comes to mind are the Coils, but even then the core 2E Coils in large replaced the core 1E Coils, imo.<br /> <br /> Edit: My MtA comment was about including gamelines in general. The God-Machine was carefully not mentioned at all in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-04-2017, 08:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T07:59:42-07:00","id":1087692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1087602#post1087602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've learned to separate what I like and what I don't like, and DTF and the God machine are not in my personal &amp;quot;canon&amp;quot;, which has allowed me to enjoy CoD the way I used to, even 2E content. My hope is that they don't make the God Machine so omnipresent throughout the CoD that it becomes too difficult to ignore it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good news, the God-Machine is intentionally kept optional. The only mention of it in Requiem 2e is in connection to one of the many potential origins of VII. There are no mentions of it at all in Forsaken or Awakening 2e as far as I recall. Created 2e has a sidebar about what connection, if any, exists between the Principle and the God-Machine, mostly because it's something a lot of fans asked for. At any rate, the existence of Descent and the God-Machine shouldn't ruin your Vampire game any more than the existence of Awakening and the Exarchs ruins it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:00:07-07:00","id":1088043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1087602#post1087602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remembered started a thread a while back where asked a question about Requiem where I forgot to specify that I wanted info on 1E. I let slip that I was wary of 2E because of the &quot;God Machine&quot;. I said that my problem was that it effectively made the rest of the WoD a sci-fi (or whatever people wish to call it) where in every setting we now had to accept that just behind the curtain there was a bunch of nuts and bolts that were controlling everything. It was kind of like when you watch a movie with a twist you think is lame, you really enjoyed the rest of the movie,but now you have to judge the whole flick based on the twist, which ruins the whole movie. I was also looking forward to Demon: the Descent, which I hoped would effectively expand on the Inferno demons,and correct the problems with the Fallen, instead we got something which I found... really weird. It would have been fine as something of an AI splat (&quot;Robot: The Activated&quot;? &quot;Android: The Programmed&quot;?) but as demons it was just too weird, even for WoD at its most creative. In both oWoD and CoD the splats are still fundamentally the same as their mythological/folklore inspirations, vampires are still vampires, werewolves are still werewolves and so on, but the same cannot be said of demons in DTF.<br /> <br /> I've learned to separate what I like and what I don't like, and DTF and the God machine are not in my personal &quot;canon&quot;, which has allowed me to enjoy CoD the way I used to, even 2E content. My hope is that they don't make the God Machine so omnipresent throughout the CoD that it becomes too difficult to ignore it.<br /> <br /> That said there are still reasons to play 1E: you may want to make use of a lot of the wealth of content built up throughout 1E and most of the stuff exclusive to 2E can be ignored or replaced, easier than adapting a whole bunch of 1E stuff to 2E. Basically, depending on how much content from 1E you want to make use of it might just be easier to go full 1E. Then there's also the question of source-books like Inferno, one of my personal favorites, which from what I understand is 100% incompatible with 2E rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If <b>God Machine</b> and <b>Demon: the Descent</b> were their own completely separate game line, I would have been happy to give them a try. But as part of the Chronicles of Darkness, they really don't fit right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Only reason I even have the GMC is because it was included as part of the 2nd edition core book, instead of being a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:19:56-07:00","id":1088054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088043#post1088043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If <b>God Machine</b> and <b>Demon: the Descent</b> were their own completely separate game line, I would have been happy to give them a try. But as part of the Chronicles of Darkness, they really don't fit right. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like it's not just your personal opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:27:46-07:00","id":1088057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088054#post1088054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say that like it's not just your personal opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Undead Parasites. Otherworldly Spirits. Creatures of Dreamstuffs. Enlightened Mystics. Frankenstein's Monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> .... <i>Transdimensional Robots!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T19:51:23-07:00","id":1088066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088057#post1088057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Undead Parasites. Otherworldly Spirits. Creatures of Dreamstuffs. Enlightened Mystics. Frankenstein's Monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> .... <i>Transdimensional Robots!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And they don't fit because...?<br /> <br /> The only reason I see why people think they don't fit together is the Magic vs. Science aesthetic that's been prevalent in some of the more famous works of fiction, which I consider exactly that; an aesthetic. No more, no less.<br /> <br /> And hey guys, I thought we were in a Vampire forum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:09:59-07:00","id":1088076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088066#post1088066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they don't fit because...?<br /> <br /> The only reason I see why people think they don't fit together is the Magic vs. Science aesthetic that's been prevalent in some of the more famous works of fiction, which I consider exactly that; an aesthetic. No more, no less.<br /> <br /> And hey guys, I thought we were in a Vampire forum?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is the reason why I say they don't fit, yes. And I was merely explaining that in my previous post. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I got into WoD because I wanted a modern day supernatural setting, and the GMC (optional, though it may be), almost ruined that for me. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, though, whether you play 1st, 2nd or mix and match edition is a matter of preference, I would guess. Personally, I prefer 1st edition, since what I've heard about 2nd either doesn't sit right with me, or just felt like an unnecessary change to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:26:33-07:00","id":1088081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088076#post1088076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got into WoD because I wanted a modern day supernatural setting, and the GMC (optional, though it may be), almost ruined that for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must have hated the blue book stuff which had sci-fi conspiracy stuff like government experiments, psychic powers, and Men in Black then? Mortals games were very X-files, and X-files was full of sci-fi and supernatural stuff without any aesthetic or thematic clashes.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't transdimensional robots anymore than werewolves are spirit-cops. Demons are fallen angels. Their god just happens to run off alien physics rather than being a wizard because things made by Gods must be physics not spells or they aren't really Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-04-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:35:21-07:00","id":1088083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088057#post1088057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Undead Parasites. Otherworldly Spirits. Creatures of Dreamstuffs. Enlightened Mystics. Frankenstein's Monsters.<br /> <br /> <br /> .... <i>Former Servants of an Uncaring Demiurge!</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for ya.<br /> <br /> (Also, where'd you get transdimensional? It's like you haven't even read Demon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T20:38:31-07:00","id":1088085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088083#post1088083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, where'd you get transdimensional? It's like you haven't even read Demon.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly angels are transdimensional, being able to travel between coordinates on whichever dimension concerns &quot;Materialness&quot;. But they lose most of that when they get cut off from God and have to shove their essence into the closest meat-suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T21:02:34-07:00","id":1088092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088085#post1088085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly angels are transdimensional, being able to travel between coordinates on whichever dimension concerns &quot;Materialness&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by this. If you're talking about the fact that they are ephemeral entities and are typically Twilight but can Materialize, that's not dimensional travel. In either case they are present in the material world, they are just shifting between states of Ephemera. If you're talking about them traveling instantly from one location in physical space to another without crossing the intervening space, that's not traveling between different dimensions, it's just a very efficient means of travel within one dimension. I guess arguably you could say it's using 4th-and-higher spatial dimensions and spacial folding, but that's a different meaning of the word dimension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-05-2017, 12:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T21:23:52-07:00","id":1088095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088092#post1088092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess arguably you could say it's using 4th-and-higher spatial dimensions and spacial folding, but that's a different meaning of the word dimension.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was using the spatial meaning of dimension. Being out of phase is basically just moving on dimension m, while keeping t,x,y,z identical. It was the only way I could see them being described as Transdimensional beings without it being a pointless statement or incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-05-2017, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T22:46:19-07:00","id":1088112,"title":"","content":"The God Machine and Demons fit in the Chronicles of Darkness better than this conversation fits in this thread. Moving along.<br /> <br /> Anybody remember any rules in 1e that were innovative and useful that were left on the cutting room floor, not replaced with something better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T03:54:15-07:00","id":1088185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088081#post1088081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You must have hated the blue book stuff which had sci-fi conspiracy stuff like government experiments, psychic powers, and Men in Black then? Mortals games were very X-files, and X-files was full of sci-fi and supernatural stuff without any aesthetic or thematic clashes.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't transdimensional robots anymore than werewolves are spirit-cops. Demons are fallen angels. Their god just happens to run off alien physics rather than being a wizard because things made by Gods must be physics not spells or they aren't really Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, I don't play mortals; I went straight for the monsters. In fact, <i>I almost never</i> play a pure human in any role playing setting I find myself in. Also, in fact, my first play through of any game that gives me the option is going to be a villain who tries to wipe out humanity (or at least mess up its world as much as possible). And I don't consider psychic powers to be in the realm of sci-fi, nor do government experiments have to strictly fall into that category, either. It's quite possible for the people in charge to take an interest in the occult, especially when they have entire task forces specifically created to hunt it down.<br /> <br /> As for the men in black, the book seems to indicate they are supernatural in some capacity, as well. Being that they have solid black eyes and generate an aura of fear. That doesn't sound like a typical government agent, to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>To Charlaquin:</b> I haven't read Demon, actually. I wasn't interested in God Machine, so I saw absolutely no reason to pick up a game that specifically caters to it. But the idea that I got from reading through GMC is that it is some kind of hyper advanced technology that exists on multiple different planes simultaneously. It also specifically talks about <i>building</i> servants, like the angels. And how they're <i>deactivated</i> when the GMC has no use for them. Pretty hard not to immediately think robot / android / cyborg when reading words like that. And Demons came across as the <i>Ghost in the Machine</i> who managed to obtain sentience and became a rogue AI.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-05-2017, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T04:34:41-07:00","id":1088198,"title":"","content":"All the &quot;sci-fi&quot; stuff around the God-Machine is basically just aesthetics. It's a sentient <i>something</i> and dressing it in terms of programming, occult matrices, constructing/deactivating angels, etc. is just a way to visualise it and create a terminology so you can talk about it.<br /> It's just as supernatural, mystical and scientific as Supernal magic, the Principle, and Sekhem sorcery.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm not trying to convince you to like the God-Machine or DtD. I'm just clarifying it. You might still dislike it and that's fine. Smaken \u00e4r som baken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-05-2017, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:04:32-07:00","id":1088210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088112#post1088112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine and Demons fit in the Chronicles of Darkness better than this conversation fits in this thread. Moving along.<br /> <br /> Anybody remember any rules in 1e that were innovative and useful that were left on the cutting room floor, not replaced with something better?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more a question that there is just so much more content out for 1E already, if you want to use a lot of content from the 1E sourcebooks it may just be easier to just do the whole thing in 1E rather than spending the time translating all of it to 2E. And again, like I mentioned before, there is the problem of books like Inferno, which just don't work with the new rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088185#post1088185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>To Charlaquin:</b> I haven't read Demon, actually. I wasn't interested in God Machine, so I saw absolutely no reason to pick up a game that specifically caters to it. But the idea that I got from reading through GMC is that it is some kind of hyper advanced technology that exists on multiple different planes simultaneously. It also specifically talks about <i>building</i> servants, like the angels. And how they're <i>deactivated</i> when the GMC has no use for them. Pretty hard not to immediately think robot / android / cyborg when reading words like that. And Demons came across as the <i>Ghost in the Machine</i> who managed to obtain sentience and became a rogue AI.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the God Machine and Demon. I get the feeling it was thought up in part to avoid drama. You see, the original Demon: The Fallen was criticized for being too &quot;Christian-centric&quot;, in other words; the lore drew too heavily from Judaeo/Christian theology as-opposed to other faiths/mythologies for some people's liking. Something tells me these complaints would be more vocal (but probably still a minority) if it were published today. This left the publishers with a dilemma: risk having these complaints with the new version or try to expand the background lore to be more inclusive.<br /> <br /> The problem with things like demons/angels/God, as opposed to other supernaturals, is that they are far more relevant to things many people believe in today, often very strongly. There's often a paranoia about offending these beliefs whenever you portray them in fiction. If they expanded the base of real world religions they drew on it would, in their eyes, run the risk of upsetting more people.<br /> <br /> It's only a theory of mine, but I can't help but wonder that the writers went with the weird techno-thriller angle because they were afraid of navigating the minefield that comes with addressing religious themes: &quot;Does this mean God exists in WoD? if so, which God? How will our religious readers react if we get things wrong? Will our non-religious readers be put off by the suggestion some religions might actually be true?&quot;<br /> <br /> I hope this isn't the case and they were just being creative, but I still wonder if that was part of the reason they chose such a different path than what people like me were expecting (and hoping for). In any case people who would complain about the above things would be a very small minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:26:48-07:00","id":1088218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088210#post1088210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's more a question that there is just so much more content out for 1E already, if you want to use a lot of content from the 1E sourcebooks it may just be easier to just do the whole thing in 1E rather than spending the time translating all of it to 2E. And again, like I mentioned before, there is the problem of books like Inferno, which just don't work with the new rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to the God Machine and Demon. I get the feeling it was thought up in part to avoid drama. You see, the original Demon: The Fallen was criticized for being too &quot;Christian-centric&quot;, in other words; the lore drew too heavily from Judaeo/Christian theology as-opposed to other faiths/mythologies for some people's liking. Something tells me these complaints would be more vocal (but probably still a minority) if it were published today. This left the publishers with a dilemma: risk having these complaints with the new version or try to expand the background lore to be more inclusive.<br /> <br /> The problem with things like demons/angels/God, as opposed to other supernaturals, is that they are far more relevant to things many people believe in today, often very strongly. There's often a paranoia about offending these beliefs whenever you portray them in fiction. If they expanded the base of real world religions they drew on it would, in their eyes, run the risk of upsetting more people.<br /> <br /> It's only a theory of mine, but I can't help but wonder that the writers went with the weird techno-thriller angle because they were afraid of navigating the minefield that comes with addressing religious themes: &quot;Does this mean God exists in WoD? if so, which God? How will our religious readers react if we get things wrong? Will our non-religious readers be put off by the suggestion some religions might actually be true?&quot;<br /> <br /> I hope this isn't the case and they were just being creative, but I still wonder if that was part of the reason they chose such a different path than what people like me were expecting (and hoping for). In any case people who would complain about the above things would be a very small minority.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It was my understanding the entire meta-plot to World of Darkness revolved around the Judaeo/Christian theology.<br /> <br /> <br /> And one might say that in Requiem, they didn't do too much better. The Judaeo/Christian vampires get an entire covenant all to themselves. But as for any other religious group (wiccan, hindu, buddhism, shinto, voodoo, est)? Meh, just toss them all in with the <i>Circle of the Crone</i> and call it a day. Don't forget to point out that they're involved in ritualistic sacrifices and blood orgies! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-05-2017, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T05:45:18-07:00","id":1088221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088218#post1088218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It was my understanding the entire meta-plot to World of Darkness revolved around the Judaeo/Christian theology.<br /> <br /> <br /> And one might say that in Requiem, they didn't do too much better. The Judaeo/Christian vampires get an entire covenant all to themselves. But as for any other religious group? Meh, just toss them all in with the <i>Circle of the Crone</i> and call it a day. Don't forget to point out that they're involved in ritualistic sacrifices and blood orgies! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to avoid to be honest, much of the Gothic fiction WoD was inspired by, including Vampires, was itself based in Christian European folklore, in which the conflict between God and Satan was said to affect everything. I guess the writers were just worried it would be a bigger problem with a new Demon game because demons and angels actually appear in the Holy Books of many religions.<br /> <br /> As Charlaquin and others have said, the God Machine can be easily ignored, which for players like me is good. I just hope we get a 2E Inferno some time in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:06:34-07:00","id":1088234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088218#post1088218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one might say that in Requiem, they didn't do too much better. The Judaeo/Christian vampires get an entire covenant all to themselves. But as for any other religious group (wiccan, hindu, buddhism, shinto, voodoo, est)? Meh, just toss them all in with the <i>Circle of the Crone</i> and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of those, probably only wiccan and voodoo would be incorporated into the circle of the crone. Shinto fits into the Ume House convenant of Japan not Circle of the Crone.<br /> <br /> In Requiem, covenants are different depending on what part of the world you're in. If you go to India, you might find that the main covenants are a hinduism based one, a bhuddism based one, and a caste based covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-05-2017, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T06:26:44-07:00","id":1088245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088221#post1088221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's hard to avoid to be honest, much of the Gothic fiction WoD was inspired by, including Vampires, was itself based in Christian European folklore, in which the conflict between God and Satan was said to affect everything. I guess the writers were just worried it would be a bigger problem with a new Demon game because demons and angels actually appear in the Holy Books of many religions.<br /> <br /> As Charlaquin and others have said, the God Machine can be easily ignored, which for players like me is good. I just hope we get a 2E Inferno some time in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, that's the option I chose to with. Just chucked the GMC completely. Doesn't exist, never did exist, never will exist in my games.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically, Masquerade seemed to be more diversified in the vampire mythos, being that the 13 clans and their respective bloodlines had elements from all over the world, rather than focusing on the European interpretations. Though I am to understand some of these <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">interpretations</span></span></span> were... shall we say 'extremely racist?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:02:36-07:00","id":1088264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088185#post1088185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>To Charlaquin:</b> I haven't read Demon, actually. I wasn't interested in God Machine, so I saw absolutely no reason to pick up a game that specifically caters to it. But the idea that I got from reading through GMC is that it is some kind of hyper advanced technology that exists on multiple different planes simultaneously. It also specifically talks about <i>building</i> servants, like the angels. And how they're <i>deactivated</i> when the GMC has no use for them. Pretty hard not to immediately think robot / android / cyborg when reading words like that. And Demons came across as the <i>Ghost in the Machine</i> who managed to obtain sentience and became a rogue AI.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that certainly explains your misunderstandings of Demons and the God-Machine. You don't have to like them, but its pretty impolite to spread misinformation about it when you haven't actually read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T07:56:56-07:00","id":1088288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088210#post1088210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's more a question that there is just so much more content out for 1E already, if you want to use a lot of content from the 1E sourcebooks it may just be easier to just do the whole thing in 1E rather than spending the time translating all of it to 2E. And again, like I mentioned before, there is the problem of books like Inferno, which just don't work with the new rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In regards to the God Machine and Demon. I get the feeling it was thought up in part to avoid drama. You see, the original Demon: The Fallen was criticized for being too &amp;quot;Christian-centric&amp;quot;, in other words; the lore drew too heavily from Judaeo/Christian theology as-opposed to other faiths/mythologies for some people's liking. Something tells me these complaints would be more vocal (but probably still a minority) if it were published today. This left the publishers with a dilemma: risk having these complaints with the new version or try to expand the background lore to be more inclusive.<br /> <br /> The problem with things like demons/angels/God, as opposed to other supernaturals, is that they are far more relevant to things many people believe in today, often very strongly. There's often a paranoia about offending these beliefs whenever you portray them in fiction. If they expanded the base of real world religions they drew on it would, in their eyes, run the risk of upsetting more people.<br /> <br /> It's only a theory of mine, but I can't help but wonder that the writers went with the weird techno-thriller angle because they were afraid of navigating the minefield that comes with addressing religious themes: &amp;quot;Does this mean God exists in WoD? if so, which God? How will our religious readers react if we get things wrong? Will our non-religious readers be put off by the suggestion some religions might actually be true?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I hope this isn't the case and they were just being creative, but I still wonder if that was part of the reason they chose such a different path than what people like me were expecting (and hoping for). In any case people who would complain about the above things would be a very small minority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to negate your theory, but avoiding controversy was never a factor in creating Demon. Not directly using Judeo-Christian symbolism was a creative choice by the developers because of how they wanted to frame the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-05T08:37:11-07:00","id":1088307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1088288#post1088288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry to negate your theory, but avoiding controversy was never a factor in creating Demon. Not directly using Judeo-Christian symbolism was a creative choice by the developers because of how they wanted to frame the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a relief, I guess I get a little too paranoid about artists self-censoring themselves because of stuff that's happened to other things I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T13:14:54-07:00","id":1094925,"title":"","content":"Yesterday i had my usual weekly Forsaken game in which one of my players constantly complains on Chrod in favor of NWoD and might as well make my weekly annoyance into something useful and he does bring a couple of good points:<br /> <br /> Point #1: Putting mechanic to things that shouldn't have mechanics. For example, interdisciplinary specialty allows you to use your medicine specialty of say, anatomy, when doing targeting attacks.<br /> <br /> In NWoD this doesn't exist, i think, but in a game with reasonable people a player can say to the DM &quot;hey look, i got a specialization to anatomy, can i get a bonus when i am attacking a specific body part&quot;<br /> <br /> Now in Chrod, there is merit that does this and a cost with requirements so now is more difficult to do the same. Because as DM, if i allow this i am cheating by giving the merit for free to a player and the one that did pay for it feels rip off. As DM is one thing having to make a judgement on the fly on things that dont have a mechanic for, and quite another going using the same when the mechanic is actually there.<br /> <br /> I used the example of Interdisciplinary specialty but there quite more of them like mentor, which makes you arbitrarily choose 3 skills (or resource) that the mentor can help your character which is something than in his mind should not have rules and be handle it on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> Point #2 The door system feels unnatural and non intuitive.Again putting mechanics in something that should be handle with 1 roll and RP.<br /> <br /> Point #3 Aspirations. They are hard to grasp and not for everyone. In my case i am close to just drop the entire concept and just assign 4 beats per session flat because they are a handful to handle on both the DM and Player side.<ul><li>Player side: Some players are passive, they dont know or cant think about what they want to happen or are more gamist and prefer to &quot;win&quot; and thus both prefer the approach of DM throws plot and you deal with it. Other many players also dont read the rules, the just come to play and asking them to think about were the game is going is too much work at best.</li> <li>DM side: Is hard to fill in the space of 4 hours of gaming, assuming 3 players, 6 aspiration + the plot that are already in motion and come to fruition on that particularly game + the ones that also come to fruition but the player dont know about. And as aspiration are tied to XP then you, as DM, feel obligated to include them first because otherwise the player will feel cheated out of XP.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-20-2017, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T05:08:01-07:00","id":1095088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1094925#post1094925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y<br /> DM side: Is hard to fill in the space of 4 hours of gaming, assuming 3 players, 6 aspiration + the plot that are already in motion and come to fruition on that particularly game + the ones that also come to fruition but the player dont know about. And as aspiration are tied to XP then you, as DM, feel obligated to include them first because otherwise the player will feel cheated out of XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually give the players the hint to align some of their aspirations with the ongoing storyline or I align the ongoing storyline to their aspirations. I think aspirations are a call-out to the storyteller saying: &quot;This is what I want the game to be about.&quot;. CofD is very close to Fate Core, but still keeping the core of the original WoD game in place. It's a lot more narrative than before and also for the first time fulfills the promise &quot;Storyteller System&quot;. The tools that CofD offers are designed to arrive at emerging game play at the table instead of scripted adventures. And the &quot;Reap the Whirlwind&quot; Jumpstart really delivers on that promise with the way the adventure is structured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:14:22-07:00","id":1095215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1095088#post1095088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually give the players the hint to align some of their aspirations with the ongoing storyline or I align the ongoing storyline to their aspirations. I think aspirations are a call-out to the storyteller saying: &quot;This is what I want the game to be about.&quot;. CofD is very close to Fate Core, but still keeping the core of the original WoD game in place. It's a lot more narrative than before and also for the first time fulfills the promise &quot;Storyteller System&quot;. The tools that CofD offers are designed to arrive at emerging game play at the table instead of scripted adventures. And the &quot;Reap the Whirlwind&quot; Jumpstart really delivers on that promise with the way the adventure is structured.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like i said, some players arent into that kind of gameplay. They want to sit down and for the player to throw situations at them and they deal with it. Some are paralyzed by choice, other just cant think outside of a gamist perspective of &quot;how to win&quot; and other just dont like that meta aspect and prefer to be all IC (meaning affecting the narrative is metagaming to them).<br /> <br /> As you said, normally one could try to move the aspirations towards the ongoing situations but other times say at the start of a new &quot;Chapter&quot; (when the PC think of new aspirations) on the campaign the snowball momentum of other storylines the player dont know about have to come to fruition and difficult to mesh that with the 6 aspiration.<br /> <br /> I mean it wouldnt be that bad if it wasnt just a tool but is so tied to character advancement that is difficult to not use it if it doesnt fit with the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-21-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T13:57:59-07:00","id":1095230,"title":"","content":"Could the problem not be fixed by the ST offering a list of aspirations that fit the intended plot to the players that aren't eager to create their own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T14:50:22-07:00","id":1095250,"title":"","content":"Or you could just skip it altogether and hand out a few extra end-of-session beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T15:33:38-07:00","id":1095263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1094925#post1094925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yesterday i had my usual weekly Forsaken game in which one of my players constantly complains on Chrod in favor of NWoD and might as well make my weekly annoyance into something useful and he does bring a couple of good points:<br /> <br /> Point #1: Putting mechanic to things that shouldn't have mechanics. For example, interdisciplinary specialty allows you to use your medicine specialty of say, anatomy, when doing targeting attacks.<br /> <br /> In NWoD this doesn't exist, i think, but in a game with reasonable people a player can say to the DM &quot;hey look, i got a specialization to anatomy, can i get a bonus when i am attacking a specific body part&quot;<br /> <br /> Now in Chrod, there is merit that does this and a cost with requirements so now is more difficult to do the same. Because as DM, if i allow this i am cheating by giving the merit for free to a player and the one that did pay for it feels rip off. As DM is one thing having to make a judgement on the fly on things that dont have a mechanic for, and quite another going using the same when the mechanic is actually there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, allowing a player to use a Specialty on a Skill it's not associated with is ouside the system rules whether or not there's a Merit that specifically allows it. Creating a Merit for it gives an in-system way to make this possible. If you would prefer this to be something anyone can do without having to buy a Merit, you can easily just make that houserule and remove Interdisciplinary Specialty as a Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1094925#post1094925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used the example of Interdisciplinary specialty but there quite more of them like mentor, which makes you arbitrarily choose 3 skills (or resource) that the mentor can help your character which is something than in his mind should not have rules and be handle it on a case by case basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merits with specific mechanical effects &gt; Merits with vague non-effects that the ST has to resolve by fiat. Both on the player side (you know exactly what you can count on your own abilities to do) and on the ST side (less need to improvise the effects of your players' abilities yourself). But if you really don't like these specific rules, you can always ignore them and run the Merit on pure fiat if you prefer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1094925#post1094925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point #2 The door system feels unnatural and non intuitive.Again putting mechanics in something that should be handle with 1 roll and RP.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been pages of advice written on how to run this system smoothly. At the end of the day though, if you don't like it, just don't use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1094925#post1094925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point #3 Aspirations. They are hard to grasp and not for everyone. In my case i am close to just drop the entire concept and just assign 4 beats per session flat because they are a handful to handle on both the DM and Player side.<ul><li>Player side: Some players are passive, they dont know or cant think about what they want to happen or are more gamist and prefer to &quot;win&quot; and thus both prefer the approach of DM throws plot and you deal with it. Other many players also dont read the rules, the just come to play and asking them to think about were the game is going is too much work at best.</li> <li>DM side: Is hard to fill in the space of 4 hours of gaming, assuming 3 players, 6 aspiration + the plot that are already in motion and come to fruition on that particularly game + the ones that also come to fruition but the player dont know about. And as aspiration are tied to XP then you, as DM, feel obligated to include them first because otherwise the player will feel cheated out of XP.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Easy solution: give a fixed number of Beats per session and leave Aspirations out of it.<br /> <br /> There's kind of an underlying theme to these critiques: too many mechanics for things that don't need mechanics. But the thing is, everyone has different standards for what needs mechanics, and different thresholds for how many is too many. And it's always easier to ignore mechanics you don't like than to invent mechanics for things you feel need them and don't have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-21-2017, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T15:50:29-07:00","id":1095266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1095263#post1095263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you would prefer this to be something anyone can do without having to buy a Merit, you can easily just make that houserule and remove Interdisciplinary Specialty as a Merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Merits with specific mechanical effects &gt; Merits with vague non-effects that the ST has to resolve by fiat. Both on the player side (you know exactly what you can count on your own abilities to do) and on the ST side (less need to improvise the effects of your players' abilities yourself). But if you really don't like these specific rules, you can always ignore them and run the Merit on pure fiat if you prefer.<br /> <br /> <br /> There have been pages of advice written on how to run this system smoothly. At the end of the day though, if you don't like it, just don't use it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Easy solution: give a fixed number of Beats per session and leave Aspirations out of it.<br /> <br /> There's kind of an underlying theme to these critiques: too many mechanics for things that don't need mechanics. But the thing is, everyone has different standards for what needs mechanics, and different thresholds for how many is too many. And it's always easier to ignore mechanics you don't like than to invent mechanics for things you feel need them and don't have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you dont like the way the some merits are written and prefer the previous version, and would have to check each one of them individually and make a ruling. Dont like the way the game make rules for things you believe shouldnt have. Dont like the Door system and neither the aspiration system. Instead of removing all of that you could cut the middle man and just play NWoD.<br /> <br /> Me personally, i prefer the more specific mechanical effects for merits, i prefer Chrods but i can see why one could prefer NWoDs if one preffers a more improv style to DM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1095250#post1095250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could just skip it altogether and hand out a few extra end-of-session beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking 4 beats per session + all the Beats they get from conditions + all the beats from Converting failures to Dramatic ones.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 05-21-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:13:41-07:00","id":1095273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1095263#post1095263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's always easier to ignore mechanics you don't like than to invent mechanics for things you feel need them and don't have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a great way to put it. Even in non-modular RPGs this is the case. Just make sure everyone in the group knows what's been removed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1075440-reasons-to-run-1st-edition-vampire?p=1095266#post1095266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking 4 beats per session + all the Beats they get from conditions + all the beats from Converting failures to Dramatic ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aspirations are supposed to grant an average of 2-3 Beats each session so that would be the amount of end-of-session Beats if you want XP gain to be unchanged. (Not accounting for Obsessions or Totem Aspirations from the specific gamelines.) However, my group wants a quicker XP progression so we use both Aspirations (2-3 Beats/session) and end-of-session Beats (most commonly 3 Beats/session, but sometimes 5 if we do a lot during the session or if we didn't get much opportunity to roll dice), meaning we'd grant ~6 end-of-session Beats if we did away with Aspirations.<br /> My point is that you should worry more about how quick you want your players to gain XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}